  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Product**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining FrogeClose. It\'s an AI agent designed for automated financial close processes in SaaS companies. My focus is on the outcome-based approach: FrogeClose needs to deliver board-ready packages with minimal human intervention. I will be sure to integrate details like autonomous month-end/quarter-end capabilities, and address that it applies to the mid-market.\n\n\n**Refining the Deliverables**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the outputs. The system will deliver a fully reconciled close package and board deck based on user inputs. The goal is to provide these to the user in a few formats, including Markdown, PDF-ready HTML, and structured JSON. The UI is being refined, incorporating a \"Run Close\" button, a progress indicator, an outcome score, and an estimate of time saved. I think I\'m doing a good job with the frontend, keeping it minimal and in dark-mode.\n\n\n**Orchestrating the Backend**\n\nI\'m deep in the backend now, focusing on the agentic loop. My plan is a multi-step process: Plan, Gather, Analyze, Draft, Self-Critique, and Finalize. I\'m leaning toward Gemini with a server-side Express backend, or possibly a full Express + Vite setup using `@google/genai`. I\'m also planning a Postgres database schema and in-memory client for the prototype, including tables for organizations, users, and various logs. Security is also top of mind, with tenant isolation, encrypted storage, and PII redaction.\n\n\n**Defining the MVP**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about what the MVP of FrogeClose should include. I\'m focusing on the problem, solution, why now, the market, and the business model, which will all be outcome-based. I will include a plan to articulate why I, as a solo founder, am best suited to tackle this, plus the go-to-market strategy. I am also planning a competitive analysis and the long-term vision.\n\n\n"
