  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Project Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on project structure, and I\'ve observed the dependencies in `package.json`, specifically `express`, `tsx`, `@google/genai`, `lucide-react`, `motion`, and `tailwindcss`. I\'m evaluating different server integration options, weighing a dedicated `server.ts` entry point versus using Vite proxy or a full-stack approach.\n\n\n**Verifying Server Execution**\n\nI\'m now checking how the development server is running and verifying our framework guidelines. I\'ve noted the `\"dev\"` script in `package.json` uses Vite, which leads me to check the full-stack server setup. I am seeing that we have an entry point at `server.ts` that will be needed to be run using `tsx`. I see that the `metadata.json` has a placeholder, so I\'ll be updating that as well.\n\n\n**Updating HTML Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on syncing the HTML metadata with `metadata.json`. I need to ensure the `<title>`, `<meta name=\"description\">`, `og:title`, and `og:description` in `index.html` are consistent, replacing any placeholders. I\'ll use \"FrogeClose \342\200\224 Autonomous Financial Close Agent\" for the title and \"Outcome-based autonomous financial close engine that reconciles accounts, performs variance analysis, and generates board-ready packages with zero human screen time.\" for the description. Also, I\'m noting the Tailwind CSS setup and the `@custom-variant dark` rule in `src/index.css`.\n\n\n**Designing FrogeClose\'s Architecture**\n\nI\'m now designing **FrogeClose**. I\'m setting the value proposition, focusing on zero human data-entry screen time in finance. I\'ll target mid-market SaaS companies and offer outcome-based billing at $1,250 per closed period. I also need to set up the branding and mission. Additionally, I need to add typography styling. Also, I\'ll incorporate the `@custom-variant dark` rule in `src/index.css` right after importing Tailwind. I will also incorporate typography styling, using fonts like Plus Jakarta Sans or DM Sans for general text and JetBrains Mono for tabular data.\n\n\n**Defining FrogeClose\'s Process**\n\nI\'ve detailed FrogeClose\'s workflow, starting with data ingestion using OCR and semantic search, all stored within a `pgvector` knowledge base. Next, I plan for autonomous planning and algorithmic reconciliation and difference detection across various financial sources. My design includes a deterministic execution DAG and tool invocation graphs.\n\n\n**Defining FrogeClose\'s Stages**\n\nI\'ve outlined FrogeClose\'s further stages. I\'m focusing on variance and runway analysis, setting automated triggers for natural language root cause analysis. I\'m also now designing the automated package drafting which includes a GAAP income statement, balance sheet, and a cash flow statement, as well as an executive memo. I am now also designing for an autonomous self-critique loop to ensure the quality and consistency of the finalized output, and an outcome billing and quality score.\n\n\n**Detailing FrogeClose\'s Outputs**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the artifacts generated by **FrogeClose**. I\'m detailing the screen-time saved, outcome pricing fees, and I\'m planning for downloadable Markdown, exportable PDF-ready HTML, a structured JSON API payload, and CSV ledger exports. I am also planning the UI and multiplayer angle.\n\n**Expanding FrogeClose\'s Roles**\n\nI\'m expanding **FrogeClose** to incorporate multi-role UI options. The roles I am adding are Controller/Finance VP with full access, an external Audit Partner with read-only access and cryptographic audit trail, and Board Observer/CEO with high-level summaries. I\'m also now designing a \"Human-in-the-Loop Exception Inbox\" to handle edge cases. I\'m also adding a Postgres schema to include `organizations` and `users`.\n\n\n**Defining Database Schemas**\n\nI\'m now detailing the database schemas. I\'m focusing on adding tables for `jobs`, `job_steps`, `files`, `audit_logs`, `billing_events`, `evaluation_results`, and `knowledge_base`. I\'m especially focused on the data within each table, and I am also adding a real Gemini API integration via Express server `/api/run-close` and `/api/agent-query` with a high-fidelity SaaS financial close simulation if the API key is unset.\n\n\n\n**Configuring Full-Stack Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the full-stack server setup. I\'m focusing on configuring `server.ts` with Express and mounting `vite.middlewares` for development, and updating the `package.json` scripts. I\'ve switched the \"dev\" script to `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` and I\'m ensuring the server runs on port 3000, adhering to environment constraints.\n\n\n"
