  }
  planner_response {
    response: "### How FrogeClose Works: The Autonomous Close Walkthrough\n\nFrogeClose flips the standard B2B SaaS model on its head: **it replaces the 80 hours a finance team spends clicking inside ERPs with a single outcome specification.**\n\n---\n\n### The End-to-End Execution Flow\n\n```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 1. High-Level Outcome Specification                                                                  |\n|    \"Close Q3 2026 books across Stripe, NetSuite GL, and SVB operating accounts. Reconcile revenue,   |\n|     run ASC 606 ratable waterfall, flag variances >10%, and synthesize 1-page board summary.\"        |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                                                  |\n                                                  v\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 2. Autonomous Multi-Step Agent Loop (Finite State Machine)                                           |\n|    - Step 1 [PLAN]: Decomposes close into a 6-node deterministic execution DAG.                     |\n|    - Step 2 [GATHER]: Retrieves ASC 606 & capitalization policies from pgvector (cos_sim > 0.91);   |\n|                       ingests and normalizes 5,128 records from Stripe, NetSuite, SVB & Brex.         |\n|    - Step 3 [RECONCILE]: Matches 5,126 items automatically (99.96% tie-out rate).                    |\n|    - Step 4 [ANALYZE]: Computes budget variances; pinpoints GPU inference spike (+20.2%) vs revenue. |\n|    - Step 5 [DRAFT]: Compiles GAAP 3-statement model, ASC 606 waterfall & board memo.                |\n|    - Step 6 [SELF-CRITIQUE]: Programmatic verification of 14 GAAP invariants (Debits == Credits).    |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                                                  |\n                                                  v\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 3. Human-in-the-Loop Exception Inbox (Modern Digital Workforce Paradigm)                            |\n|    Humans are never forced to do repetitive data entry. When a true anomaly occurs (e.g. an          |\n|    unmatched $18,450 AWS upfront charge), it is surfaced with an autonomous suggested journal       |\n|    entry. One click by the Controller approves it, updating the ledger and sealing the audit hash.   |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                                                  |\n                                                  v\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 4. Board-Ready Deliverables & Outcome-Based Billing                                                 |\n|    - Outcome Quality Score: 98.4 / 100                                                               |\n|    - Screen Time Saved: 74.5 hours                                                                   |\n|    - Outcome Pricing: $1,250 charged only on successful close (vs. $14,800 manual cost)              |\n|    - Exportable: Download Markdown, Print/PDF Deck, Export Audit JSON payload                        |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n### Core Artifacts Included in the Codebase\n\n1. **Working Minimalist UI (`src/App.tsx`):**\n   - **Outcome Header:** Live Outcome Score (0\342\200\223100), Screen Time Saved Counter, Outcome Pricing vs. Legacy Cost, Verified ARR ($24.8M), and Runway (28.5 mo).\n   - **Goal Console & Connected Sources:** 3 one-click presets + drag-and-drop source files (Stripe, NetSuite GL, SVB PDF, Brex CSV).\n   - **Agent State Machine Stepper:** Inspect tool calls (`pgvector_semantic_search`, `reconcile_bank_vs_ledger`, `calculate_budget_variances`, `audit_accounting_invariants`), reasoning logs, and latency.\n   - **Institutional Deliverables View:**\n     - **Executive Board Memo:** Board-ready Markdown with unit economics and retention commentary.\n     - **GAAP Reconciled P&L:** Subscription vs. usage revenue, COGS, GM% (81.4%), Operating Income (+$426k), Net Income.\n     - **ASC 606 Waterfall:** Ratable amortization schedule across July, August, and September.\n     - **Variance Attribution Table:** Filterable by materiality with autonomous root-cause commentary.\n     - **Exception Review Inbox:** Controller approval workflow that updates the ledger in real-time.\n     - **Audit Trail:** Immutable, SHA-256 chained event log for PwC / EY audit verification.\n   - **Role Switcher:** Switch between **Controller (Admin)**, **External Auditor (PwC)**, and **Board Observer (VC)**.\n2. **`README.md`:** YC-caliber thesis covering Problem, Solution, Why Now, Market ($8.1B TAM), Outcome Pricing, GTM, and Solo Founder leverage.\n3. **`SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`:** Mermaid architecture diagram, complete PostgreSQL 16 schema with Row-Level Security (RLS) policies, `pgvector` indexing, and tool sandboxing.\n4. **`PITCH.md`:** One-page YC / a16z Speedrun pitch memo on \"The End of the Screen Time KPI.\"\n5. **`EVALUATION.md`:** Concrete evaluation criteria (100% Debit-Credit balance integrity, $<0.01\\%$ error tolerance, screen time reduction metrics).\n\n---\n\n### 3 Key Architecture Suggestions for FrogeClose\n\n1. **Deterministic Sandboxing for Financial Invariants:**\n   - *Why:* Probabilistic LLMs should never be allowed to do arithmetic directly in their output tokens. \n   - *Recommendation:* Keep the current pattern where Gemini generates reasoning and natural language attribution, while an isolated Python/Wasm sandbox executes the double-entry balance check ($\\sum \\text{Debits} \\equiv \\sum \\text{Credits}$).\n2. **Tenant-Isolated Vector Memory (`pgvector` + RLS):**\n   - *Why:* Every mid-market company has bespoke accounting quirks (e.g. custom multi-year contract renewals or capitalization thresholds). \n   - *Recommendation:* Store each company\'s approved exception resolutions and accounting policy memos in `pgvector` with strict Row-Level Security (`tenant_id = current_setting(\'app.current_org_id\')`). This creates an insurmountable data moat.\n3. **Stripe Metered Outcome Billing Webhook:**\n   - *Why:* To fulfill the vision of outcome pricing, wire the final state transition (`FINALIZE` / `SELF_CRITIQUE_PASSED`) directly to Stripe Usage-Based / Invoiced Billing via an idempotency key, billing $1,250 only when the 14 GAAP invariants pass."
    modified_response: "### How FrogeClose Works: The Autonomous Close Walkthrough\n\nFrogeClose flips the standard B2B SaaS model on its head: **it replaces the 80 hours a finance team spends clicking inside ERPs with a single outcome specification.**\n\n---\n\n### The End-to-End Execution Flow\n\n```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 1. High-Level Outcome Specification                                                                  |\n|    \"Close Q3 2026 books across Stripe, NetSuite GL, and SVB operating accounts. Reconcile revenue,   |\n|     run ASC 606 ratable waterfall, flag variances >10%, and synthesize 1-page board summary.\"        |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                                                  |\n                                                  v\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| 2. Autonomous Multi-Step Agent Loop (Finite State Machine)                                           |\n|    - Step 1 [PLAN]: Decomposes close into a 6-node deterministic execution DAG.                     |\n|    - Step 2 [GATHER]: Retrieves ASC 606 & capitalization policies from pgvector (cos_sim > 0.91);   |\n|                       ingests and normalizes 5,128 records from Stripe, NetSuite, SVB & Brex.         |\n|    - Step 3 [RECONCILE]: Matches 5,126 items automatically (99.96% tie-out rate).                    |\n|    - Step 4 [ANALYZE]: Computes budget variances; pinpoints GPU inference spike (+20.2%) vs revenue. |\n|    - Step 5 [DRAFT]: Compiles GAAP 3-statement model, ASC 606 waterfall & board memo.                |\n|    - Step 6 [SELF-CRITIQUE]: Programmatic verification of 14 GAAP invariants (Debits == Credits).    |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+