  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Visualize Expenditure**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started integrating Recharts into `src/App.tsx`. I\'m focusing on the \'variance\' tab right now. The idea is to visualize Actual vs Budget expenditures using a BarChart. I\'m building out the data structure for the comparison now.\n\n\n**Refine Data Structure**\n\nI\'ve got the initial data structure ready for the visualization of actual versus budget expenditures. It includes categories, actual amounts, budget amounts, variance, percentage differences, and display-formatted values.  I\'m now thinking about how to handle different views, such as line item versus department, and will introduce tabs or toggles accordingly.\n\n\n**Implement Tooltip**\n\nI\'ve integrated a custom tooltip component into the visualization for the expenditure data. It displays category labels, actual versus budget values formatted with \'k\' notation, and shows the difference with color-coding for over or under budget. This provides clear and concise information upon hovering over the bar chart elements.\n\n\n**Incorporate Visuals**\n\nOkay, I\'m now integrating the Recharts bar chart into the \'variance\' tab, right above the detailed table. I\'ve imported the necessary Recharts components and am working on displaying the budget/actual comparison. I\'m also adding metric summary cards for an overview and a mode switcher for different views. I think it is important to also incorporate the custom tooltip to allow for interactive data exploration.\n\n\n"
