  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Chart Views**\n\nI\'m currently focused on adding a new state variable, `varianceViewMode`, to the chart. This will let users switch between viewing variance data by either individual \"categories\" like Hosting or Legal, or by broader \"departments\" such as COGS or R&D. This should offer more flexibility for data analysis.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Structure**\n\nNow I\'m diving deeper into the sample expenditure data. I\'m taking a close look at the \'department\' and \'name\' fields, so I can more clearly determine how the chart data can be effectively grouped and presented. My goal is a clear delineation between the individual categories and the higher-level departments. This is for effective implementation of the variance view.\n\n\n**Refining Data Grouping**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the practical application of the \'department\' field within the variance view. I\'m examining how to display the data to align with the \'department\' groupings. My main focus is on how the chart data can reflect the department and category. I want to ensure the data is clearly and flexibly grouped.\n\n\n**Implementing Tooltips**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on implementing a custom tooltip for the Recharts component. I\'ve built a `CustomVarianceTooltip` to display both actual and budgeted figures, as well as the variance, within the chart. The tooltip is designed to show department information and also use a consistent visual style, which improves the user\'s data interpretation.\n\n\n**Adding Chart Modes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the ability to toggle the chart view between \'category\' and \'department\' modes. I\'ve introduced a `chartMode` state variable, which will allow users to dynamically switch between viewing data at different granularities. My focus is on the integration of this new state with the chart\'s rendering to ensure a smooth user experience.\n\n\n**Designing Chart Elements**\n\nI\'m now building out the chart\'s visual structure. I\'m focusing on the \"By Line Category\" and \"By Department Rollup\" controls to facilitate toggling between views. I\'m incorporating quick summary indicators for Total OpEx & COGS and using color-coding (amber for over-budget, emerald for under-budget) for quick insights. I\'m also configuring the `ResponsiveContainer` to be 300px in height, and configuring `BarChart`, `CartesianGrid`, `XAxis`, `YAxis`, `Tooltip`, `Legend` and `Bar` to display the actual data.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_381269"
