  planner_response {
    response: "### Integrated Recharts Bar Chart in the Variance Attribution Tab\n\nThe **Variance Attribution** tab now features an interactive **Recharts bar chart** that visually contrasts **Actual vs. Approved Budget** expenditures:\n\n---\n\n### Key Features Added\n\n1. **Dual Visual Modes (Category & Department Rollup):**\n   - **Category Breakdown:** Side-by-side comparison across key cost drivers:\n     - *Cloud Hosting (AWS)*: Actual **$342.5k** vs. Budget **$285.0k** (+20.2% variance)\n     - *Sales Commissions*: Actual **$495.0k** vs. Budget **$410.0k** (+20.7% variance)\n     - *Customer Support*: Actual **$284.0k** vs. Budget **$290.0k** (-2.1% favorable)\n     - *Dev Infrastructure & Staging*: Actual **$320.0k** vs. Budget **$310.0k** (+3.2% variance)\n     - *Legal & Audit Compliance*: Actual **$112.0k** vs. Budget **$135.0k** (-17.0% favorable)\n   - **Department Rollup:** Aggregated view across **COGS** ($1,154k vs $1,080k), **R&D** ($2,150k vs $2,200k), **S&M** ($1,680k vs $1,590k), and **G&A** ($790k vs $825k).\n2. **Executive Expenditure Metric Strip:**\n   - Total OpEx + COGS Actual (**$5,774,000**)\n   - Approved Budget (**$5,695,000**)\n   - Net Expenditure Variance (**+$79,000 / +1.4%**)\n   - Invariant verification status (**Audit Balanced**)\n3. **High-Fidelity Dark Mode Tooltip:**\n   - Displays exact dollar figures in tabular numerals (`tabular-nums`), department tags, and color-coded variance deltas (emerald for favorable savings, amber for overages).\n4. **Clean Zero-Pill Aesthetic:**\n   - Uses rounded `[4, 4, 0, 0]` bars with high contrast (Emerald `#10b981` for actuals, Slate `#475569` for approved budget)."
