  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Unified Documents**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing `PITCH.md`, `SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`, `README.md`, and `EVALUATION.md` to ensure complete alignment after the unified 1-page pitch memo. My focus is on verifying that these documents now fully reflect the updated Problem, Solution, Why Now, Target Customer, Pricing, Moat, Competition, and Traction elements. This is vital to ensure comprehensive consistency.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_564339"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"# FrogeClose (FrogeClose.com): YC & a16z Speedrun 1-Page Pitch Memo\\n\\n**Company:** FrogeClose (FrogeClose.com)  \\n**One-Line Description:** AI closes the books; the controller only reviews exceptions. Outcome-based financial close engine for mid-market SaaS.  \\n**Founder:** Yogesh Bhatt, B.Sc. CSIT student, Kathmandu. Built this prototype solo.  \\n**Stage:** Functional prototype tested on synthetic multi-source data with deterministic code verification.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Problem\\nEvery high-growth mid-market SaaS company ($5M to $100M ARR) loses 10 to 18 business days every month closing their books. Senior controllers spend 60\342\200\223100 hours copy-pasting Stripe payouts into spreadsheets, matching bank wire receipts, tracking deferred revenue waterfalls under ASC 606, and amortizing sales commissions under ASC 340-40. Companies spend $150k+/year on internal controllers and outsourced CPA firms for repetitive, manual tie-outs prone to formula breakage.\\n\\n### 2. Solution\\nFrogeClose kills the screen-time KPI: **AI closes the books; the controller only reviews exceptions.**  \\nThe finance team connects their stack (Stripe + NetSuite/QBO + Bank CSVs). FrogeClose parses, reconciles, and evaluates 5 deterministic code-computed GAAP invariants. The controller only inspects flagged edge-case exceptions with proposed journal entries.\\n\\n### 3. Why Now?\\n1. **Long-Context Window & Multimodal Parsing:** Models can now ingest 5,000+ line general ledgers, raw Stripe webhooks, and PDF bank statements in a single reasoning loop.\\n2. **Deterministic Sandboxing:** By strictly separating AI classification from deterministic arithmetic code execution, agents can now perform accounting without hallucinating numbers.\\n\\n### 4. Target Customer\\nMid-market B2B SaaS companies ($5M\342\200\223$100M ARR) using Stripe + NetSuite or QuickBooks Online + Silicon Valley Bank / Mercury. The entry wedge is the month-end close package and one-page executive board memo.\\n\\n### 5. Business Model & Outcome Pricing\\n100% outcome-based billing: **$1,250 per successful monthly close**.  \\n- Zero seat licensing lock-in.\\n- **Risk-free guarantee:** If mathematical invariants fail ($\\\\sum \\\\text{Debits} \\\\neq \\\\sum \\\\text{Credits}$), the customer pays $0.\\n- Unit economics: Compute and LLM inference cost is ~$0.18\342\200\223$0.45 per run, yielding high software gross margins while saving the customer $12k+/mo in manual accounting costs.\\n\\n### 6. The Moat: Institutional Accounting Memory (`pgvector`)\\nEvery SaaS business has bespoke accounting policies (e.g. custom multi-year contract renewals, capitalization thresholds under ASC 350-40, and commission amortization schedules under ASC 340-40). FrogeClose stores every approved journal entry and exception resolution in tenant-isolated vector memory. Switching away means losing the institutional memory of how the company accounts for its contracts.\\n\\n### 7. Competition & Differentiation\\n- **FloQast / BlackLine:** Checklist and Excel-sync tools that still require humans to perform every reconciliation by hand.\\n- **Numeric:** Modern close workspace, but still designed around maximizing human screen time.\\n- **Rillet:** Modern ERP, but requires migrating away from NetSuite/QBO entirely (high friction).\\n- **FrogeClose:** Sits on top of existing stacks (NetSuite, QBO, Stripe) and autonomously generates the reconciled package while humans only review exceptions.\\n\\n### 8. Traction & Transparency\\n- Functional working prototype with real CSV ingestion and deterministic code checks.\\n- Conducted discovery interviews with SaaS controllers to map the Stripe-to-GL tie-out bottleneck.\\n- **Target:** 3 mid-market SaaS design partner pilots ($5M\342\200\223$25M ARR) to run parallel month-end closes.\\n\\n### 9. The Ask\\nLooking for design partners and pre-seed backing to scale native ERP connectors and conduct pilot closes with 3 SaaS finance teams.\\n\", \"Description\":\"Update PITCH.md with unified 1-page memo and honest founder positioning\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/PITCH.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating PITCH.md\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update unified PITCH.md\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\242\006\n\237\006\001i\024}\023q\266i\326\005\237<\223\320\230\323aRH\242d)\016\371\303\2642\336\253\313v\\\261T\364\250\0165\370F\272\241\226C\030\210A\372\311s~\324\257\341\217\350\345x\237\210\362B\226kRh\225\205\202\363\2675\347\023\373\341\336\347\370%\252\036$b\372\3436\367}\021[\247\367j\372\267\265\004wb+;.\330\317\373\277l\257\356\361f\277\261|Z\201{O.\321\257Q\201\322b\215\211\\sq\220\022\352\352/kk\241\352\020dJ\270\322o\344\326\255V\311\004\270KK\366\b\371{vD\342\351\200\233\353\300=\0061\245\300?\265\263\335H\277m\231;\206\031\006\313K\221r\247\344\362\344\360\377B\323\024n\023\aN\200)\302H\274\374\317\\&W\a\223\rL\311\235\251\230\370j_\336\201\372[\310*{\r\n\210\v+\233w}5\030\\d\270,\225\321e\203u.\271&^\271B\302Aj\237\245g\261\241\301\032\336#E\005?\354W\001U\237\255\250\264q\032b\2165\353\t\246\337\325\324+\002\367\324\256\254\202rob\2029\244\020\201\326\325\351\347\337\230] \024\320\331\24064t;qF\253\245\341\035\334U\257\336\b\037R\271G\351\203\ag\206\346\030@\211:\024-\267\020\263t}\205\034\311<\325\334\226J2r\243YY.\247\346;\3754\360\272\270IZz\022\364\207#i\331h\253\316Ud:\330\347\345\016\223\352\335\2528Q\221\305\215\225n\362\312y\021\027\214e;%\375-[p\221Cr\343\221\342\310\247\030\006R\bGVP\034 \031\ry\226>\241/\231\025O\222\356\270\257~\353o\347\2711yO\272\002\306\202\221Ud\022\006\224\227\275\244\003\0051=\003\377c{~\226\351\rF<\214]\001\236G\023mw+\206\025\023\241\vf3E6Ik+\253:\"+\275\220\367\260\243\305<\001c;\360Xc\262\333\270\270\326\v\232\264\336\240z(\034\322\020\320GC\335\b0\322\344\274\270=\332\002\374\252\262\vV^\353L\n\327\276\375\236\216Y\323\251\346\212W\272\350D\a\031\fw\t\266\262\353\202w\215\362\346\373/iX\"\307\306[\263\270\301\333\0352\037\243\267\353\360\342\205>g\037>\360\225\321\023A@n\235c\271\251(\234\2109\345\230?z\330X\276\265\222\022t\004\"\345\303\343\220\376\213\2353\204\221\362E\001\307\242\'\220\343\032\242J@k\332s\351\261\210\376\301\301\207\334\244\203q\271\023\003[\305\2005\263Kl[\025\243\260+6\272Pfn[\250B\375\3165\306L_\350\3416c\276\r\305E\037\355\370\344!\b\251\003!\264\213\247Qu\035\255\203C\2742\345\016\201\330*\r=\304\241\372D#\\H\233\277\346\310\0021\244\003\020\277\330\324\030\320\261\314Q\215\367\034c\'\213X\300\234\345\2063VT\034\320\375:\330\322i\033\333\301vh\256\224\316\254\347\321s\037(R\035\004"
