            }
            lines {
              text: "### 1. The Thesis: The Death of the Screen Time KPI"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "For fifteen years, the holy grail of SaaS was screen time. The more minutes a finance manager spent inside NetSuite or QuickBooks, the more software companies could charge for seats."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "**AI reverses this dynamic completely.**  "
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "As a16z noted in *\342\200\234The End of the Screen Time KPI in AI Applications,\342\200\235* the highest-value AI systems will be evaluated on how **little** humans have to interact with them. "
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "FrogeClose replaces the 80 hours a controller spends copy-pasting Stripe payouts into spreadsheets with a single prompt:  "
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "> *\342\200\234Close Q3 2026 books, reconcile Stripe + SVB, run variance analysis, and generate our board package.\342\200\235*"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "The agent executes the entire pipeline, verifies all mathematical invariants, and returns finished deliverables. Humans only review exceptions."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "### 2. The Customer Pain & Market Size"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Mid-Market SaaS ($5M to $100M ARR):** Too large for simple automated bookkeeping (Bench, Pilot), yet too small to staff a 15-person accounting department."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **The Close Nightmare:** The average mid-market SaaS takes 14 days to close the books every month. High-paid CFOs ($250k\342\200\223$400k) spend their first two weeks of every quarter acting as glorified data-entry clerks instead of strategic capital allocators."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **TAM:** Over 45,000 mid-market SaaS and tech-enabled businesses in the US and Europe spending an average of $180,000/year on accounting salaries and outsourced close firms = **$8.1B TAM** for autonomous financial close alone."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_DELETE
