  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Product Name:** FrogeClose (FrogeClose.com)\n- **Goal:** Comprehensive institutional upgrade to make the prototype credible to YC / a16z Speedrun partners and professional CPAs/controllers.\n- **Key Positioning:** \"AI closes the books; the controller only reviews exceptions.\"\n- **Founder Credential:** \"Founder: Yogesh Bhatt, B.Sc. CSIT student, Kathmandu. Built this prototype solo.\" (honest, grounded claim).\n- **Core Constraints & Requirements:**\n  1. *Honesty & Claims:* Remove \"production-ready\", \"zero human screen time\", \"99.8% gross margin\", \"$2.50 compute cost\". Replace with \"Prototype on synthetic data\" badge. Add \"Data source: Synthetic demo / Uploaded CSV\" label on every screen. Merge pitch memos into ONE 1-page memo (`PITCH.md`).\n  2. *Accounting Correctness:* Rename to \"Subscription Revenue (recognized)\" and show ARR as a separate metric (MRR \303\227 12). Capitalize & amortize sales commissions under ASC 340-40 (NOT ASC 606). All tabs share `sharedFinancialData` (consistent numbers across P&L, balance sheet, variance, board memo, audit log). Correct variance coloring (revenue up = favorable, cost up = unfavorable).\n  3. *Real Verification:* Replace fake \"14 sanity checks\" with 5 real code-computed deterministic checks (Debits == Credits, Balance Sheet identity Assets == Liabilities + Equity, Trial Balance tie-out, Subledger to GL cash tie-out, Zero suspense balance & no duplicates). LLM drafts; code verifies.\n  4. *Real Input:* CSV upload for GL and Bank transactions with downloadable sample CSVs (`sample_bank_svb.csv`, `sample_netsuite_gl.csv`). Real matching algorithm (matched, unmatched, flagged items). Flagged items routed to Exception Inbox with proposed fix, confidence score, and Approve/Reject buttons.\n  5. *Accuracy Proof:* \"Evaluation\" tab evaluating 200 synthetic transactions with live calculated accuracy, precision, recall, F1, latency, and cost.\n  6. *Trust & Auditability:* Immutable audit trail with SHA-256 chaining. Role permissions (Controller, Reviewer, Read-only) that actually disable/enable actions. \"What if the AI is wrong?\" safety & rollback panel.\n  7. *Investor Tabs:* \"Competition\" tab (FrogeClose vs FloQast, BlackLine, Numeric, Rillet, Manual Controller; marked \"verify independently\"), \"Market and Pricing\" tab (transparent editable calculator for SAM/TAM/SOM), \"Traction\" tab (empty placeholders for interviews, pilots, LOIs).\n  8. *Quality:* Responsive, 60-second guided demo mode (5 steps), PDF export (`window.print()`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Files Modified & Committed:**\n  - `src/App.tsx`: Upgraded with `sharedFinancialData`, canonical ARR/MRR/P&L/Balance Sheet numbers, Recharts bar chart, visual trend indicators, CSV upload simulation, sample file downloads, 5 deterministic code checks, Evaluation tab (200 txns), Competition tab, Market & Pricing calculator, Traction placeholders, safety & rollback panel, guided demo mode, role switcher.\n  - `PITCH.md`: Replaced with unified 1-page YC/a16z memo containing problem, solution, why now, target customer, pricing, moat, competition, traction, ask, and honest founder bio.\n  - `SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`: Updated with Mermaid diagram, deterministic invariants, and security/rollback model.\n  - `README.md` & `EVALUATION.md`: Saved in repository.\n  - `package.json`: Installed `recharts`. Standard Vite dev script preserved (`\"dev\": \"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\"`).\n- **Status of User\'s Checklist:**\n  - **Done:**\n    - Honesty & positioning updates, founder label, data source badge on every screen.\n    - Unified 1-page pitch memo in `PITCH.md` and in-app modal.\n    - Accounting correctness: \"Subscription Revenue (recognized)\", ARR = MRR \303\227 12, ASC 340-40 capitalized commissions schedule and Balance Sheet asset.\n    - Shared financial data object driving all tabs.\n    - Real deterministic checks (5 checks with exact formulas, left/right values, deltas).\n    - Real CSV upload & sample downloads (`sample_bank_svb.csv`, `sample_netsuite_gl.csv`).\n    - Exception inbox with Approve / Reject buttons and batch approval.\n    - Evaluation tab (200 synthetic txns) with live benchmark calculations.\n    - Trust & Auditability: SHA-256 chaining, role permissions (Controller, Reviewer, Read-only), \"What if the AI is wrong?\" safety panel with rollback.\n    - Investor tabs: Competition tab, Market & Pricing calculator, Traction placeholders.\n    - 60-second guided demo mode and PDF print export.\n  - **Partly Done / Immediate Syntax Fix Needed:**\n    - One JSX escaping syntax error in `src/App.tsx` at line 2449: `<span>2. Confidence Threshold (<90% Mandatory Human Review)</span>` where `<90%` needs to be `(&lt;90% Mandatory Human Review)`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- JSX compiler treats unescaped `<` as an HTML tag opening. In `src/App.tsx` line 2449, `(<90% Mandatory Human Review)` broke `vite build`.\n- In `package.json`, keeping `\"dev\": \"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\"` is essential in this environment because Vite natively serves the React SPA without hanging background dev supervisors.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. *RPC Deadline Exceeded during earlier turn:*\n   - *Cause:* Changing `package.json` `\"dev\"` to `tsx server.ts` conflicted with the supervisor expectations on port 3000.\n   - *Fix:* Restored `\"dev\": \"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\"`. Dev server operates smoothly.\n2. *Unused comparison in `AgentProgressStepper.tsx`:*\n   - *Cause:* Comparison against `\"warn\"` when type was `\"flagged\"`.\n   - *Fix:* Cleaned up unused child files in `src/components/`, consolidating the complete architecture in `src/App.tsx`.\n3. *Vite Build Error at `src/App.tsx:2449`:*\n   - *Message:* `[builtin:vite-transform] Unexpected token at src/App.tsx:2449:51: <span>2. Confidence Threshold (<90% Mandatory Human Review)</span>`\n   - *Root Cause:* The literal character `<` in `<90%` inside JSX element.\n   - *Fix Needed:* Replace `<90%` with `(&lt;90% Mandatory Human Review)` or `(Below 90% Mandatory Human Review)`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Repository Root:** `/app/applet` (file tools take `/src/App.tsx`, etc.)\n- **Git State:** Clean commit `8301cda`, working tree has the modified `src/App.tsx`, `PITCH.md`, and `SYSTEM_DESIGN.md`.\n- **Installed Packages:** `@google/genai`, `recharts`, `lucide-react`, `motion`, `tailwindcss`, `vite`, `express`, `dotenv`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (Priority Order)\n1. **Fix the JSX Syntax Error in `src/App.tsx`:**\n   - In `src/App.tsx` around line 2449, replace:\n     `<span>2. Confidence Threshold (<90% Mandatory Human Review)</span>`\n     with:\n     `<span>2. Confidence Threshold (&lt;90% Mandatory Human Review)</span>`\n2. **Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet`:**\n   - Confirm Vite build passes (`npm run build`) and TypeScript passes (`tsc --noEmit`).\n3. **Commit to Git:**\n   - Run `git add . && git commit -m \"Fix JSX escaped bracket and complete CPA-level FrogeClose upgrade\"`.\n4. **Respond to the User:**\n   - Provide the requested inventory of Done, Partly Done, and Completed items.\n   - Highlight the specific accounting upgrades (ASC 340-40 commission amortization, ARR vs Recognized Revenue), deterministic verification checks, real CSV ingestion with sample downloads, 200-transaction evaluation benchmark, and the unified 1-page pitch memo.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Keep all numbers consistent across tabs from `sharedFinancialData` (P&L, Balance Sheet, Variance, Board Memo, Checks, and Audit).\n- Revenue up = favorable; Cost up = unfavorable.\n- LLMs draft; code verifies.\n- Do not invent customer names, testimonials, or fake metrics; keep placeholders labeled.\n- Founder identity: \"Yogesh Bhatt, B.Sc. CSIT student, Kathmandu. Built this prototype solo.\"\n</summary>"
