    captured_user_requests {
      text: "You are an elite product engineer, AI architect, and Y Combinator application coach. \n\nBuild a complete, production-minded prototype of *CloseRun* \342\200\224 the outcome-based AI agent that performs autonomous month-end / quarter-end financial close and produces board-ready packages for mid-market SaaS companies with almost zero human screen time.\n\n### Core Vision (YC-style)\nFor the last 15 years, software success was measured by screen time. CloseRun kills that KPI. \nA finance team describes the desired outcome once (\342\200\234Close Q3 books, reconcile these sources, produce variance analysis + one-page board summary\342\200\235). CloseRun plans, executes, self-critiques, and returns polished deliverables. Users pay only for successful outcomes. This is the exact shift described in a16z\342\200\231s \342\200\234The end of the screen time KPI in AI applications.\342\200\235\n\n### Target Customer & Wedge\nMid-market SaaS companies ($5M\342\200\223$100M ARR) using modern stacks (Stripe + QuickBooks Online / NetSuite + Google Drive / Excel / Notion). \nFirst job-to-be-done: Turn source files + system connections into a fully reconciled close package + board deck.\n\n### Full System Design (must be reflected in the code and documentation)\n\n*Architecture*\n- Frontend: Extremely minimal dark-mode UI (Next.js style, but generate clean HTML/JS/Tailwind that can be moved to Next.js + Vercel later). One goal input, file upload zone, \342\200\234Run Close\342\200\235 button, progress indicator, results panel with downloadable artifacts, outcome score, time-saved estimate, and mock outcome-based price.\n- Backend / Agent Orchestration: Multi-step agentic loop (Plan \342\206\222 Gather \342\206\222 Analyze \342\206\222 Draft \342\206\222 Self-Critique \342\206\222 Finalize) using Gemini 1.5/2.x Pro with strong tool use and long context. Use a state machine pattern.\n- Database: Postgres schema (users/orgs, jobs, job_steps, files, audit_logs, billing_events, evaluation_results, knowledge_base).\n- Vector Store: pgvector (or equivalent) for company-specific knowledge, past successful closes, and semantic retrieval of policies/charts of accounts.\n- File Storage: Abstracted object storage (S3-compatible).\n- Background Jobs: Long-running agent executions must be asynchronous.\n- Security (non-negotiable):\n  - Tenant isolation with Row Level Security\n  - Encrypted file storage\n  - Tool sandboxing for code execution\n  - Full audit log of every tool call and model decision\n  - PII detection + redaction options\n  - Rate limiting and cost controls per organization\n- Observability: Every step, confidence score, and failure must be logged for evaluation.\n\n*Agent Behavior (must implement)*\n1. User states high-level outcome + uploads files or pastes data.\n2. Agent creates a detailed plan.\n3. Gathers and structures data (CSV/PDF/DOCX/images via OCR).\n4. Performs reconciliation, variance analysis, calculations.\n5. Drafts the full deliverable package (reconciled P&L, variance commentary, one-page board summary).\n6. Self-critiques for accuracy, completeness, and professional quality.\n7. Finalizes and returns downloadable Markdown + PDF-ready HTML + structured JSON.\n8. Shows Outcome Score (0\342\200\223100), estimated time saved, and \342\200\234This successful close would cost $X under outcome pricing.\342\200\235\n\n*Data Structures & Algorithms (show technical depth)*\n- Use appropriate structures for job state (finite state machine), file metadata, and step history.\n- Efficient reconciliation algorithms (matching, difference detection).\n- Semantic search over vector embeddings for company knowledge.\n- Confidence scoring and self-critique loops.\n\n*Workforce / Multiplayer Angle*\nDesign the system so multiple parties (finance team, external accountants, board) can later review the same run with proper permissions. The agent acts as a digital workforce that produces the outcome while humans only review exceptions.\n\n### What You Must Generate\n\n1. *Working prototype code*  \n   - Clean, self-contained frontend (dark mode, minimal, outcome-focused).  \n   - Backend simulation of the full multi-step agent (use Gemini tool-calling patterns).  \n   - Mock database interactions and vector retrieval.  \n   - Security comments and RLS-style checks.  \n   - Downloadable outputs and outcome pricing indicator.\n\n2. *README.md* (YC application quality)  \n   - Problem, Solution, Why Now, Market, Why Solo Founder can win, Business Model (outcome-based), Go-to-Market, Competition, Vision.\n\n3. *System Design Document*  \n   - Architecture diagram in text/Mermaid.  \n   - Database schema.  \n   - Security model.  \n   - Evaluation harness criteria (how we measure real outcome quality).\n\n4. *One-page YC / a16z pitch*  \n   Written exactly as if applying to YC or a16z Speedrun. Emphasize the end of screen-time KPI, outcome pricing, and the vertical wedge.\n\n5. *Suggested evaluation criteria*  \n   Concrete metrics for success rate, accuracy, time saved, and human review burden.\n\nStart by scaffolding the full working app code that I can run and iterate on inside Google AI Studio, then export to Next.js + Vercel. Make every design decision production-minded so a YC partner reading the code + README would say \342\200\234this founder already thinks like a scaled company.\342\200\235\n\nBegin now. App name FrogeClose .com ask me if you have any suggestion for my app so that i can best refine the architecture for scalability and user experience."
    }
