      text: "Continue from where you stopped. Do not rewrite or remove anything already built. First, list which items from my previous request are done, which are partly done, and which are not started. Then finish the remaining items in order, and keep all numbers consistent across tabs.You are a senior full-stack engineer and a CPA-level finance product lead. Upgrade the FrogeClose app so it is credible to YC and a16z Speedrun investors and to real controllers. Keep the current dark UI style. Make all of the changes below.\n\n1. HONESTY AND CLAIMS\n- Remove \"production-ready\", \"zero human screen time\", \"99.8% gross margin\" and \"$2.50 compute cost\". Replace them with a clear \"Prototype on synthetic data\" badge.\n- Replace \"Elite Product Engineer & AI Architect\" with a placeholder: \"Founder: [Name], B.Sc. CSIT student, Kathmandu. Built this prototype solo.\"\n- Reframe the positioning as: \"AI closes the books; the controller only reviews exceptions.\"\n- Add a \"Data source: Synthetic demo / Uploaded CSV\" label on every screen.\n- Merge the two pitch memos into ONE one-page memo: problem, solution, why now, target customer, pricing, moat, competition, traction, ask.\n\n2. ACCOUNTING CORRECTNESS\n- Rename \"Subscription ARR (Ratable ASC 606)\" to \"Subscription Revenue (recognized)\". Show ARR as a separate metric (MRR x 12).\n- Treat sales commissions correctly: capitalize and amortize them under ASC 340-40 and show a small amortization schedule. Fix the pitch text that wrongly says ASC 606 for CAC.\n- Make all numbers consistent across tabs: the P&L, variance table, board memo and audit trail must pull from one shared data object.\n- Color favorable and unfavorable variances correctly (revenue up = favorable, cost up = unfavorable).\n\n3. REAL VERIFICATION\n- Replace the fake \"14 sanity checks\" with real deterministic checks computed in code: debits = credits, trial balance ties to the statements, balance sheet balances, subledger ties to GL, no duplicate journal entries. Show pass/fail per check with the actual numbers.\n- Never let the LLM mark its own work as passed. The LLM drafts; code verifies.\n\n4. REAL INPUT\n- Add a CSV upload for a general ledger and bank transactions. Provide a downloadable sample CSV.\n- Run reconciliation (matching bank vs ledger) on the uploaded data and show matched, unmatched and flagged items.\n- Send only the flagged items to the Exception Inbox with a proposed fix, a confidence score, and Approve / Reject buttons.\n\n5. ACCURACY PROOF\n- Add an \"Evaluation\" tab: run the agent on 200 synthetic transactions with known correct answers. Show match accuracy, false positives, false negatives, and average time and cost per close. Compute these from the run, not hardcoded.\n\n6. TRUST AND AUDITABILITY\n- Make the Immutable Audit Trail log every agent action with timestamp, input, output, who approved, and a hash of the previous entry.\n- Add role permissions (Controller, Reviewer, Read-only) that actually change what the user can do.\n- Add a \"What if the AI is wrong?\" panel covering human override, rollback, and confidence thresholds.\n\n7. INVESTOR PAGES\n- Add a \"Competition\" tab comparing FrogeClose with FloQast, BlackLine, Numeric, Rillet and a manual controller, covering target customer, pricing, automation level and weakness. Mark clearly that the data should be verified.\n- Add a \"Market and Pricing\" tab with a transparent calculation: price per close, number of target SaaS companies, and the resulting revenue potential, with every assumption editable.\n- Add a \"Traction\" tab with empty fields for customer interviews, pilots, and letters of intent that I will fill in.\n\n8. QUALITY\n- Remove duplicate or decorative tabs that add no value.\n- Make everything responsive and fix text truncated with \"...\".\n- Add loading, error and empty states.\n- Add a 60-second guided demo mode that walks through: upload, agent runs, exceptions reviewed, board package exported.\n- Export the board package as a PDF.\n\nDo not invent customer names, testimonials, revenue or traction. If data is missing, show a clearly labeled placeholder. When done, list what you changed and anything that is still a placeholder."
    }
