  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Upload Handling**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `handleSimulateUpload` function and how it processes uploaded files. Specifically, I\'m examining the initial steps where the upload state is set, and a progress notice is initiated. The code indicates the file name is being incorporated into an upload notice, for user feedback.\n\n\n**Improving Upload Preview**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about enhancing the upload process. Now, when a file is passed to `handleSimulateUpload`, I plan to use `file.text()` to read and parse the CSV data. I\'ll extract the headers and the first five rows immediately to update the `bankPreview` or `glPreview` state. The goal is to provide instant visual feedback to the user upon file selection, and to replace the data immediately with the uploaded file data, for much better UX.\n\n\n**Refining Preview Display**\n\nI\'m now refining the preview table design, thinking about title, meta information, and the best way to display `Bank` vs `GL` data. I\'m leaning towards a tab selector or split view for \"Bank\" and \"NetSuite GL\" CSVs, including file and row counts in the labels, with a header and column data type hints for each table. The goal is a clean, user-friendly, responsive display.\n\n\n"
