  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Icon Usage**\n\nI\'m currently focused on identifying and importing necessary icons from `lucide-react`, specifically `Eye` and `Table`. I\'ve begun to consider their application. The next stage involves examining the types and helper functions associated with CSV preview functionality, specifically for the design of the `CsvPreviewData` interface. This is my key concern at the moment.\n\n\n**Defining CSV Parser**\n\nI\'ve just defined the `CsvPreviewData` interface, including `RowCount`, `headers`, `rows`, and `sourceType`. Now I\'m writing the `parseCsvToPreview` helper function, which will handle parsing the CSV data based on the provided source type. I\'m focusing on handling commas within quoted fields to ensure accurate field separation, and extracting the first six lines for preview purposes.\n\n\n**Implementing State Logic**\n\nI\'m now incorporating state management with `useState`. I\'ve initialized state for `bankPreview`, `glPreview`, and `selectedPreviewTab`, utilizing the `parseCsvToPreview` function to pre-populate data. I\'ve also implemented `handleSimulateUpload` to simulate file uploads and process the data. This updates previews based on the selected file type. I\'m ensuring proper updates of the `bankPreview` and `glPreview` states.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the UI design within the Reconciliation tab. Specifically, I plan to position the CSV preview table right after the upload dropzones. I\'m also considering adding \"Load Sample Bank Data\" and \"Load Sample GL Data\" buttons to provide quick-loading options for testing and demonstration. I have the downloadSampleFile helper from before.\n\n\n**Refining Preview Container**\n\nI\'m currently refining the UI elements. I\'ve developed a crisp preview container, styled with a dark background and subtle borders, to provide visual feedback. I\'m focusing on incorporating the `Table` icon to enhance visual clarity and ensure the design matches the application\'s overall aesthetic. The container features the structured data preview and instant schema inspection, improving the interface.\n\n\n**Analyzing Tabular Structure**\n\nI\'m presently analyzing the structure of the CSV data. I\'ve begun reviewing the headers and row counts for the bank data, confirming columns like `Transaction_ID`, `Date`, and `Amount`. I\'m going to look at adding some logic, based on the `selectedPreviewTab` state variable, to render the proper data, and to render the correct number of rows.\n\n\n**Visualizing Preview Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the detailed presentation of the preview data, starting with a clean, monospaced table. I will include row index badges and header badges to identify data types, with special highlighting for amounts based on credit or debit. I\'ll provide a badge showing the row range displayed and the total parsed entries.\n\nI\'m checking the lines in `src/App.tsx` I need to modify, specifically for the imports and the interfaces. I\'ll implement state changes to reflect preview data. I will modify `handleSimulateUpload` to use `FileReader`, call `parseCsvToPreview`, and update the preview states accordingly.\n\n\n"
