  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Structuring the Changes**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the planned changes. My plan involves updating imports in `src/App.tsx` to include `Table` and `Eye` from `lucide-react`. I will also introduce a new interface named `CsvPreviewData`. A helper function, `parseCsvToPreview`, will also be added to assist with processing CSV data.\n\n\n**Defining the CsvPreviewData**\n\nI\'ve defined `CsvPreviewData` as an interface. This includes `headers`, `rows`, and `sourceType`. Also, I\'ve created the `parseCsvToPreview` function to process CSV data, handling potential issues such as empty CSVs and parsing quoted fields correctly. The function now processes CSV data, extracting headers and a preview of the first few rows, along with calculating the total row count.\n\n\n**Implementing State Variables**\n\nI\'m now implementing state variables within the `App()` function using `useState`. I\'ve initialized `bankPreview` and `glPreview` with default CSV data using `parseCsvToPreview`. Added `activePreviewType` to manage which data previews are displayed. I\'ve also updated `handleSimulateUpload` to accept a `File` object, and handle the file read, and update the state.\n\n\n**Refining the Display Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the JSX to display the preview tables based on `activeTab` and `activePreviewType`. For the reconciliation tab, I\'m inserting the rich preview table below the upload dropzones. I\'ve designed the table to handle Bank and GL previews effectively, offering both a 2-column or stacked view for `\'both\'` and expanded views for `\'bank\'` and `\'gl\'`. I\'m also including column badges.\n\n\n"
