  }
  planner_response {
    response: "Your customer (typically a **Finance Controller, VP of Finance, or Head of Accounting** at a $5M\342\200\223$50M ARR SaaS company) can use **FrogeClose** directly in their browser. \n\nHere is how they access it and their exact end-to-end workflow:\n\n---\n\n### 1. How Your Customer Accesses the App\n\nShare your **Live App URL** with them:\n\360\237\221\211 **[Open FrogeClose in Browser](https://ais-pre-65gomtbb2qbbzavn7bygmi-467794922969.asia-southeast1.run.app)**\n\n*No installations or local setup required. It runs in any modern desktop browser.*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Choosing Their User Role\n\nAt the top right of the screen, the user can toggle between three real-world permission tiers:\n\n| Role | Permissions & Capabilities |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Controller (Full Sign-off)** | Can approve/reject exceptions, run bulk approvals, trigger the close cycle, and perform rollbacks. |\n| **Reviewer (Staff / Senior)** | Can inspect tie-outs, upload files, and propose journal adjustments. |\n| **Read-only (Auditor / Board)** | Can review financial statements, variance charts, and the immutable audit trail with write actions disabled. |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Customer Close Workflow\n\nThe core promise of FrogeClose is: **\"AI closes the books; the controller only reviews exceptions.\"** \nInstead of spending 5\342\200\2237 days manually cross-referencing spreadsheets, your customer follows these 5 steps:\n\n#### Step 1: Upload Data & Inspect Structure (`Reconciliation` tab)\n1. The customer clicks the **Reconciliation** tab.\n2. They upload two files (or click **\"Download Sample Bank CSV\"** and **\"Download Sample GL CSV\"** to test with the built-in data):\n   - **Bank Transactions CSV** (SVB, Mercury, Brex, or Stripe payout feed).\n   - **General Ledger CSV** (NetSuite or QuickBooks journal lines).\n3. **Instant 5-Row Preview**: Immediately upon uploading, they inspect the first 5 rows to confirm column headers, dates, and debit/credit alignments.\n\n#### Step 2: Run Autonomous Close (`Run Close` Hero)\n1. The customer enters or confirms their close instructions (e.g., *\"Reconcile Stripe and SVB bank deposits against NetSuite GL, recognize ASC 606 revenue, capitalize sales commissions under ASC 340-40\"*).\n2. They click the green **\"Run Close\"** button.\n3. The multi-step agent executes:\n   - Matches 5,000+ line items on amount, reference IDs, and dates.\n   - Amortizes capitalized sales commissions over 4 years under ASC 340-40.\n   - Verifies all double-entry journal entries.\n\n#### Step 3: Review Exceptions (`Exceptions` tab)\n1. Out of thousands of transactions, only items with confidence below 90% or discrepancies are surfaced to the **Exception Inbox**.\n2. For each exception (e.g., an unmapped $18,450 AWS RI prepayment), the AI suggests the exact debit/credit journal entry.\n3. The controller can:\n   - Click **Approve** on individual items.\n   - Click **Reject** to request vendor inquiry.\n   - Click **\"Approve All Pending Exceptions\"** for one-click bulk sign-off.\n\n#### Step 4: Verify Deterministic GAAP Invariants (`Sanity Checks` tab)\nTo ensure total audit compliance, **the LLM is never allowed to grade its own work**. \nThe customer goes to the **Sanity Checks** tab to see 5 hardcoded mathematical proofs:\n1. $\\sum \\text{Debits} \\equiv \\sum \\text{Credits}$ ($\\Delta = \\$0.00$).\n2. $\\text{Balance Sheet Identity: } \\text{Assets} \\equiv \\text{Liabilities} + \\text{Equity}$ ($\\Delta = \\$0.00$).\n3. **P&L to Retained Earnings** tie-out.\n4. **Operating Cash Subledger** ties directly to GL Account `#1010`.\n5. **Zero Suspense Balance** in Account `#9999`.\n\n#### Step 5: Export Board Deliverables (`Executive Board Memo` & `P&L` tabs)\n1. **Recharts Variance Attribution**: Compare actual vs. budget spending visually by category and department.\n2. **One-Page Board Memo**: Pre-drafted executive summary ready for investors or board meetings.\n3. **Export PDF**: Click the **\"Export PDF\"** button at the top header to generate a print-ready audit package.\n\n---\n\n### 4. What If the AI Makes a Mistake?\nIf your customer asks about safety or error recovery:\n- Click the **\"Safety & Error Bounds\"** button in the header.\n- **One-Click Rollback**: The controller can instantly revert the entire close cycle back to the pre-close snapshot.\n- **Cryptographic Audit Trail**: Every tool decision, match, and approval is logged with timestamp, user ID, and a SHA-256 chained block hash.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Giving a Quick 60-Second Demo\nIf your customer just wants a fast overview:\n- Have them click the **\"Guided Demo\"** button in the top navigation bar.\n- It will take them on a 5-step interactive walkthrough highlighting the goal input, the 5-row CSV preview, the exception inbox, and the board memo."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Customer Interaction**\n\nI\'m focusing on how the user\'s customer will interact with their app, FrogeClose. I\'m exploring the customer\'s perspective as a mid-market SaaS controller. My goal is to determine the optimal user experience for autonomous month-end close. I\'m prioritizing ease of use and efficiency for this role.\n\n\n**Defining Access and Roles**\n\nI\'m now clarifying how the customer interacts with FrogeClose, focusing on access and roles. I\'ve pinpointed the Shared App URL for direct browser access, perfect for the Finance Controller role. I\'m distinguishing between the Finance Controller, who oversees approval and execution, and the Reviewer, who will need some sort of access. I\'m thinking of how the \"reviewer\" may interface with the app to test. I\'m working to make this concise.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Your customer (typically a **Finance Controller, VP of Finance, or Head of Accounting** at a $5M\342\200\223$50M ARR SaaS company) can use **FrogeClose** directly in their browser. \n\nHere is how they access it and their exact end-to-end workflow:\n\n---\n\n### 1. How Your Customer Accesses the App\n\nShare your **Live App URL** with them:\n\360\237\221\211 **[Open FrogeClose in Browser](https://ais-pre-65gomtbb2qbbzavn7bygmi-467794922969.asia-southeast1.run.app)**\n\n*No installations or local setup required. It runs in any modern desktop browser.*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Choosing Their User Role\n\nAt the top right of the screen, the user can toggle between three real-world permission tiers:\n\n| Role | Permissions & Capabilities |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Controller (Full Sign-off)** | Can approve/reject exceptions, run bulk approvals, trigger the close cycle, and perform rollbacks. |\n| **Reviewer (Staff / Senior)** | Can inspect tie-outs, upload files, and propose journal adjustments. |\n| **Read-only (Auditor / Board)** | Can review financial statements, variance charts, and the immutable audit trail with write actions disabled. |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Customer Close Workflow\n\nThe core promise of FrogeClose is: **\"AI closes the books; the controller only reviews exceptions.\"** \nInstead of spending 5\342\200\2237 days manually cross-referencing spreadsheets, your customer follows these 5 steps:\n\n#### Step 1: Upload Data & Inspect Structure (`Reconciliation` tab)\n1. The customer clicks the **Reconciliation** tab.\n2. They upload two files (or click **\"Download Sample Bank CSV\"** and **\"Download Sample GL CSV\"** to test with the built-in data):\n   - **Bank Transactions CSV** (SVB, Mercury, Brex, or Stripe payout feed).\n   - **General Ledger CSV** (NetSuite or QuickBooks journal lines).\n3. **Instant 5-Row Preview**: Immediately upon uploading, they inspect the first 5 rows to confirm column headers, dates, and debit/credit alignments.\n\n#### Step 2: Run Autonomous Close (`Run Close` Hero)\n1. The customer enters or confirms their close instructions (e.g., *\"Reconcile Stripe and SVB bank deposits against NetSuite GL, recognize ASC 606 revenue, capitalize sales commissions under ASC 340-40\"*).\n2. They click the green **\"Run Close\"** button.\n3. The multi-step agent executes:\n   - Matches 5,000+ line items on amount, reference IDs, and dates.\n   - Amortizes capitalized sales commissions over 4 years under ASC 340-40.\n   - Verifies all double-entry journal entries.\n\n#### Step 3: Review Exceptions (`Exceptions` tab)\n1. Out of thousands of transactions, only items with confidence below 90% or discrepancies are surfaced to the **Exception Inbox**.\n2. For each exception (e.g., an unmapped $18,450 AWS RI prepayment), the AI suggests the exact debit/credit journal entry.\n3. The controller can:\n   - Click **Approve** on individual items.\n   - Click **Reject** to request vendor inquiry.\n   - Click **\"Approve All Pending Exceptions\"** for one-click bulk sign-off.\n\n#### Step 4: Verify Deterministic GAAP Invariants (`Sanity Checks` tab)\nTo ensure total audit compliance, **the LLM is never allowed to grade its own work**. \nThe customer goes to the **Sanity Checks** tab to see 5 hardcoded mathematical proofs:\n1. $\\sum \\text{Debits} \\equiv \\sum \\text{Credits}$ ($\\Delta = \\$0.00$).\n2. $\\text{Balance Sheet Identity: } \\text{Assets} \\equiv \\text{Liabilities} + \\text{Equity}$ ($\\Delta = \\$0.00$).\n3. **P&L to Retained Earnings** tie-out.\n4. **Operating Cash Subledger** ties directly to GL Account `#1010`.\n5. **Zero Suspense Balance** in Account `#9999`.\n\n#### Step 5: Export Board Deliverables (`Executive Board Memo` & `P&L` tabs)\n1. **Recharts Variance Attribution**: Compare actual vs. budget spending visually by category and department.\n2. **One-Page Board Memo**: Pre-drafted executive summary ready for investors or board meetings.\n3. **Export PDF**: Click the **\"Export PDF\"** button at the top header to generate a print-ready audit package.\n\n---\n\n### 4. What If the AI Makes a Mistake?\nIf your customer asks about safety or error recovery:\n- Click the **\"Safety & Error Bounds\"** button in the header.\n- **One-Click Rollback**: The controller can instantly revert the entire close cycle back to the pre-close snapshot.\n- **Cryptographic Audit Trail**: Every tool decision, match, and approval is logged with timestamp, user ID, and a SHA-256 chained block hash.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Giving a Quick 60-Second Demo\nIf your customer just wants a fast overview:\n- Have them click the **\"Guided Demo\"** button in the top navigation bar.\n- It will take them on a 5-step interactive walkthrough highlighting the goal input, the 5-row CSV preview, the exception inbox, and the board memo."
