    thinking: "**Analyzing User Request**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. My focus is now on the specific need for a React Context provider. I understand this provider should manage user authentication and authorization, effectively acting as a gatekeeper for the \"Controller\" functionality, and controlling access to \"Reviewer\" and \"Read-only\" based on roles. I\'m starting to visualize how this will fit into the existing architecture.\n\n\n**Defining User Roles & Permissions**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the permissions tied to each user role. I\'ve defined the `User` type, including properties like `id`, `name`, `email`, `role`, and `title`. Crucially, I\'m mapping roles (`controller`, `reviewer`, `read_only`) to specific actions such as approving exceptions, running closes, and uploading files. I will focus on making sure these roles cannot trigger approvals.\n\n\n**Implementing Access Control Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the access control logic, focusing on the `checkPermission` function and the `<Gate>` component. I\'m making sure `handleResolveException`, `handleRejectException`, `handleApproveAllExceptions`, and `handleRollback` functions are protected with `useAuth()`. I\'m working on disabling UI elements for reviewers and read-only users, with detailed visual cues and in-app alerts for unauthorized actions, such as locking down the \"Approve All Pending Exceptions\" button and providing tooltips on approvals or run close buttons. I\'m focusing on providing users a clear explanation.\n\n\n**Designing Onboarding Tour**\n\nI\'m now designing an interactive onboarding tour using a state machine. I\'ve defined states for the tour, including `IDLE`, `STEP_GOAL_INPUT`, `STEP_RECONCILIATION`, `STEP_EXCEPTIONS`, and `STEP_VERIFICATION`. I\'m focusing on highlighting key dashboard components. The goal is to provide a clean FSM, focusing on how controllers specify close parameters once and deterministically ingest bank statements and GL journals, how the AI surfaces anomalies requiring sign-off, and deterministic verification.\n\n\n**Developing Tour Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on fleshing out the onboarding tour. I\'ve added a `STEP_STATEMENTS` state, highlighting key dashboard areas related to financial reporting, including P&L data and Board memo. I\'m also including `STEP_ROLES_AUDIT` to highlight the Auth Role switcher and the audit trail. I\'m finalizing the `COMPLETED` state with quick action buttons. I\'m focusing on the transitions now, like the `SELECT_STEP` action that provides direct step navigation. The design will feature translucent backdrops, spotlights on key areas, and floating tour cards with step details.\n\n\n"
