    thinking: "**Analyzing Auth Permissions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `requireController` from `useAuth()` is utilized across different exception handling functions: `handleResolveException`, `handleRejectException`, and `handleApproveAllExceptions`. This suggests a centralized permissions check, and I\'m examining if this implementation is ideal. I\'m looking at potential performance implications.\n\n\n**Reviewing Audit Trail Generation**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to how audit log entries are generated upon exception approval within the controller. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the `auditEntry` object and its data fields. I want to ensure that all relevant information is captured, especially regarding the \'CONTROLLER_EXCEPTION_APPROVED\' action. The logic for generating the `current_hash` is now a primary interest.\n\n\n**Examining Exception Rejection Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `handleRejectException` function. Specifically, I\'m analyzing how exceptions are marked as rejected and how resolution notes are generated for the audit log, alongside the `auditEntry` object. I want to understand how the \'CONTROLLER_EXCEPTION_REJECTED\' action is implemented. The data being captured for this action, including `input_data` and `output_data`, is a key area of focus for me.\n\n\n**Investigating Bulk Approvals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `handleApproveAllExceptions` function, specifically the \'BULK_EXCEPTIONS_APPROVED\' action within the audit log. The logic for generating the audit entry, including `auditLogs[0]?.current_hash`, and how the `current_hash` is being handled in the context of bulk approvals is critical to my understanding. I need to know why bulk approval actions can result in a new hash value. I am focusing on what data is captured.\n\n\n**Examining Data Capture**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of the audit entry generated during bulk exception approvals. The `data` field interests me, specifically how `items_approved` and `output_data` are structured. I\'m keen to understand the `prev_hash` and `current_hash` relationship, particularly the significance of the hardcoded `current_hash` value in this case, and its connection to the overall hash generation strategy. The role of `approved_by` is also relevant.\n\n\n**Exploring State Management**\n\nMy attention has moved to the state management within `AppContent`. I\'m examining `useState` hooks, specifically `showSafetyPanel` and `demoStep`. I want to understand how these state variables are used and modified within the component. The impact of their state changes on the UI is something I\'m curious to explore in detail.\n\n\n"
