            }
            lines {
              text: "                <div><strong>Company:</strong> FrogeClose (FrogeClose.com)</div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <div><strong>Founder:</strong> Yogesh Bhatt, B.Sc. CSIT student, Kathmandu. Built prototype solo.</div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <div><strong>Stage:</strong> Functional working prototype with deterministic invariant validation.</div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <div><strong>Pricing:</strong> $1,250 per closed period (Outcome-based guarantee: $0 if debits != credits).</div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              </div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              <div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <h4 className=\"font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1\">1. The Problem</h4>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                  Every mid-market SaaS company ($5M-$100M ARR) loses 10 to 18 business days every month closing their books. Senior controllers spend 60-100 hours copy-pasting Stripe payouts into spreadsheets, matching bank wire receipts, and amortizing commissions under ASC 340-40. Companies spend $150k+/year on controller salaries and outsourced firms for repetitive data entry."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                </p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              </div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              <div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <h4 className=\"font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1\">2. The Solution</h4>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                  FrogeClose reverses the screen-time KPI: <strong>AI closes the books; the controller only reviews exceptions.</strong> The user uploads source files or connects Stripe/ERP. FrogeClose parses, reconciles, and evaluates 5 deterministic code-computed GAAP invariants. Humans only inspect flagged edge cases."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                </p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              </div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              <div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <h4 className=\"font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1\">3. Why Now?</h4>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                  Until recently, LLMs lacked the long context window and structured tool-calling required to parse 5,000+ line general ledgers alongside multi-page bank statements. Combined with deterministic code sandboxing for arithmetic, agents can now execute financial closes reliably without hallucinated math."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                </p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              </div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              <div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <h4 className=\"font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1\">4. Target Customer & Wedge</h4>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                  Mid-market SaaS ($5M-$100M ARR) using Stripe + NetSuite/QuickBooks + SVB/Mercury. The wedge is the month-end close package and one-page board summary memo. Once we reconcile the ledger, we own the financial system of truth."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                </p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              </div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              <div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <h4 className=\"font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1\">5. Business Model & Pricing</h4>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                <p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                  100% outcome-based pricing: $1,250 per successful monthly close. Zero seat fees. If mathematical invariants do not balance to the penny, the client pays $0."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "                </p>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "              </div>"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
