  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. React Context Provider for Authentication & Authorization (`AuthContext`)\n\nWe created a dedicated `AuthProvider` (`src/context/AuthContext.tsx`) and wrapped the entire application in it, creating institutional-grade role separation:\n\n- **Personas & Profiles**:\n  - **Controller (`Elena Rostova, CPA` - VP of Finance & Corporate Controller)**: Has full GAAP approval authority, rollback authority, and close execution sign-off.\n  - **Reviewer (`Marcus Vance` - Senior Accountant / FP&A)**: Can view, stage files, and propose journal adjustments, but **cannot approve exceptions or rollback**.\n  - **Read-Only (`Sarah Sterling` - Audit Committee Chair / Board Observer)**: View-only observer access.\n- **Authorization Gate (`requireController`)**:\n  - Intercepts approval attempts (`handleResolveException`, `handleRejectException`, `handleApproveAllExceptions`, and `handleRollback`).\n  - If a **Reviewer** or **Read-only** user clicks an approval or rollback button, an **Access Denied Security Modal** pops up explaining that SOX/GAAP internal control policies require Controller sign-off, with an instant button to switch to the Controller profile.\n- **Visual Gating & Feedback**:\n  - A persistent **\"Authorization Gate\"** banner displays whenever a non-controller role is active.\n  - The Exception Inbox displays lock icons (`<Lock />`) and specific badges (`[Controller Only]`) on buttons when a non-controller is logged in.\n  - The top bar displays the active user\'s initials, name, department, and role switcher dropdown.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Interactive Onboarding Tour (`OnboardingTour`) with Finite State Machine\n\nWe built an interactive onboarding overlay (`src/components/OnboardingTour.tsx`) driven by a finite state machine with keyboard support and automated tab synchronization:\n\n- **State Machine Transitions**:\n  - `START`, `NEXT`, `PREV`, `JUMP_TO_STEP`, and `DISMISS`.\n  - Supports keyboard shortcuts: `ArrowRight` (Next), `ArrowLeft` (Previous), `Escape` (Exit tour).\n- **Automated Tab Synchronization**:\n  - As the tour progresses, it calls `onTabChange()` to navigate the actual dashboard tabs in sync with the tour step, showing each component live!\n- **7-Step Walkthrough Flow**:\n  1. **Step 1: Autonomous Goal Declaration** (`Board Memo` tab) \342\200\224 Explains the outcome-based model (\"define the desired outcome once\").\n  2. **Step 2: Reconciliation & Instant 5-Row CSV Preview** (`Reconciliation` tab) \342\200\224 Explains real data ingestion and structure validation.\n  3. **Step 3: Exception Inbox & Controller Gating** (`Exceptions` tab) \342\200\224 Highlights the human-in-the-loop exception workflow and role gate.\n  4. **Step 4: Deterministic Code Invariants** (`Deterministic Verification` tab) \342\200\224 Explains why the LLM never grades its own work (Debits = Credits, Balance Sheet identity).\n  5. **Step 5: Variance Attribution & Recharts** (`Variance` tab) \342\200\224 Highlights actual vs. budget spending with QoQ trend markers.\n  6. **Step 6: ASC 340-40 Capitalization & Statements** (`Statements & ASC 340` tab) \342\200\224 Explains sales commission amortization over 48 months ($15k/quarter) vs ratable ASC 606 revenue.\n  7. **Step 7: Immutable Audit Trail & Rollback** (`Audit Trail` tab) \342\200\224 Highlights SHA-256 block chaining and one-click rollback.\n- **Interactive Tour Trigger**:\n  - Click the **\"Interactive Tour\"** button with the glowing sparkle icon in the top header to launch or replay the tour at any time.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: Passed with 0 errors.\n- `compile_applet`: Production build succeeded.\n- Git commit: `d58afcd: Add AuthContext provider with Controller authorization gate and OnboardingTour state machine`."
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed the working tree\'s cleanliness, which signifies a fresh start. Now, I\'m carefully reviewing the initial request to fully grasp the need for a React Context provider dedicated to user authentication and authorization. The primary goal is to securely gate the \"Controller\" functionality.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### 1. React Context Provider for Authentication & Authorization (`AuthContext`)\n\nWe created a dedicated `AuthProvider` (`src/context/AuthContext.tsx`) and wrapped the entire application in it, creating institutional-grade role separation:\n\n- **Personas & Profiles**:\n  - **Controller (`Elena Rostova, CPA` - VP of Finance & Corporate Controller)**: Has full GAAP approval authority, rollback authority, and close execution sign-off.\n  - **Reviewer (`Marcus Vance` - Senior Accountant / FP&A)**: Can view, stage files, and propose journal adjustments, but **cannot approve exceptions or rollback**.\n  - **Read-Only (`Sarah Sterling` - Audit Committee Chair / Board Observer)**: View-only observer access.\n- **Authorization Gate (`requireController`)**:\n  - Intercepts approval attempts (`handleResolveException`, `handleRejectException`, `handleApproveAllExceptions`, and `handleRollback`).\n  - If a **Reviewer** or **Read-only** user clicks an approval or rollback button, an **Access Denied Security Modal** pops up explaining that SOX/GAAP internal control policies require Controller sign-off, with an instant button to switch to the Controller profile.\n- **Visual Gating & Feedback**:\n  - A persistent **\"Authorization Gate\"** banner displays whenever a non-controller role is active.\n  - The Exception Inbox displays lock icons (`<Lock />`) and specific badges (`[Controller Only]`) on buttons when a non-controller is logged in.\n  - The top bar displays the active user\'s initials, name, department, and role switcher dropdown.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Interactive Onboarding Tour (`OnboardingTour`) with Finite State Machine\n\nWe built an interactive onboarding overlay (`src/components/OnboardingTour.tsx`) driven by a finite state machine with keyboard support and automated tab synchronization:\n\n- **State Machine Transitions**:\n  - `START`, `NEXT`, `PREV`, `JUMP_TO_STEP`, and `DISMISS`.\n  - Supports keyboard shortcuts: `ArrowRight` (Next), `ArrowLeft` (Previous), `Escape` (Exit tour).\n- **Automated Tab Synchronization**:\n  - As the tour progresses, it calls `onTabChange()` to navigate the actual dashboard tabs in sync with the tour step, showing each component live!\n- **7-Step Walkthrough Flow**:\n  1. **Step 1: Autonomous Goal Declaration** (`Board Memo` tab) \342\200\224 Explains the outcome-based model (\"define the desired outcome once\").\n  2. **Step 2: Reconciliation & Instant 5-Row CSV Preview** (`Reconciliation` tab) \342\200\224 Explains real data ingestion and structure validation.\n  3. **Step 3: Exception Inbox & Controller Gating** (`Exceptions` tab) \342\200\224 Highlights the human-in-the-loop exception workflow and role gate.\n  4. **Step 4: Deterministic Code Invariants** (`Deterministic Verification` tab) \342\200\224 Explains why the LLM never grades its own work (Debits = Credits, Balance Sheet identity).\n  5. **Step 5: Variance Attribution & Recharts** (`Variance` tab) \342\200\224 Highlights actual vs. budget spending with QoQ trend markers.\n  6. **Step 6: ASC 340-40 Capitalization & Statements** (`Statements & ASC 340` tab) \342\200\224 Explains sales commission amortization over 48 months ($15k/quarter) vs ratable ASC 606 revenue.\n  7. **Step 7: Immutable Audit Trail & Rollback** (`Audit Trail` tab) \342\200\224 Highlights SHA-256 block chaining and one-click rollback.\n- **Interactive Tour Trigger**:\n  - Click the **\"Interactive Tour\"** button with the glowing sparkle icon in the top header to launch or replay the tour at any time.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: Passed with 0 errors.\n- `compile_applet`: Production build succeeded.\n- Git commit: `d58afcd: Add AuthContext provider with Controller authorization gate and OnboardingTour state machine`."
