  user_input {
    user_response: "Continue the existing FrogeClose app. Do NOT delete working code. Keep the dark UI. First list what is done / partial / not started, then build everything below IN ORDER in this one session. Never invent customers, traction, revenue, or testimonials. Show a \"Prototype on synthetic data\" badge. If AI Studio cannot run something for real, implement it behind an interface, say so clearly, and output the production version (schema.sql, config) too.\n\nCODE QUALITY RULES (enforced)\n- TypeScript strict, input validation (zod) on every API route, centralized error handling, environment variables only for secrets, no secrets in frontend code.\n- ALL security checks run on the server. UI hiding is never security.\n- Write automated tests for: reconciliation, ASC 606 schedule, ASC 340-40 schedule, the 5 invariants, role permissions, tenant isolation, Stripe webhook idempotency, audit hash chain. Show test results.\n\n1. AUTH AND TENANCY: signup/login behind an AuthProvider interface (Supabase Auth or Clerk swappable), organizations, memberships, roles Controller / Reviewer / Read-only enforced server-side. Accounting-firm mode: one user manages multiple client orgs.\n2. DATABASE: schema.sql (Postgres + pgvector + Row Level Security) for orgs, users, memberships, jobs, job_steps, files, bank_transactions, ledger_entries, stripe_payouts, matches, exceptions, journal_proposals, audit_logs, billing_events, evaluation_results, knowledge_base. Every table has org_id; repository layer always filters by org_id.\n3. FILES: CSV/PDF upload with type/size limits, checksums, signed-URL-style access, PII redaction option, sample CSV downloads (bank, ledger, Stripe payouts).\n4. BACKGROUND JOBS: async closes with queued/running/succeeded/failed, retries with backoff, idempotency key per close, progress polling.\n5. AGENT STATE MACHINE: Plan, Ingest, Reconcile, Draft, Verify, Exceptions, Finalize. Log each transition with input, output, confidence, duration, cost.\n6. DETERMINISTIC ENGINE (plain code, no LLM): reconciliation (normalize, hash-join on amount + date window, score ambiguous pairs, resolve by bipartite matching); recognized revenue + deferred revenue waterfall (ASC 606); ARR = MRR x 12 shown separately; commissions capitalized and amortized (ASC 340-40); checks with real pass/fail numbers: debits = credits, trial balance ties to statements, balance sheet balances, subledger ties to GL, no duplicate entries. The LLM only classifies ambiguous items and drafts commentary. It can never mark work as passed.\n7. EXCEPTIONS AND CONFIDENCE GATING: items above the threshold auto-resolve; below go to the Exception Inbox with proposed journal entry, confidence, Approve/Reject. Human override and rollback of any resolution.\n8. AUDIT TRAIL: every action logged with timestamp, actor, input, output, approver, hash of previous entry. \"Verify chain\" button detects tampering.\n9. STRIPE (test mode): Checkout plus webhook with signature verification, billing per verified close. Bill only if all checks pass AND a Controller approves. Idempotency keys, no double charge, automatic void/refund when a check fails, invoices and usage per org, first close free.\n10. SECURITY AND COST CONTROL: per-org rate limits and cost caps, input sanitization, \"What if the AI is wrong?\" panel.\n11. OBSERVABILITY AND EVALUATION: error logging, cost and time per close. Evaluation tab: 200 synthetic transactions with known answers (about 10% deliberate problems); compute accuracy, false positives, false negatives from the run, never hardcoded.\n12. DIFFERENTIATORS:\n a) Stripe payout tie-out explaining fees, refunds, disputes, FX and timing to the cent.\n b) Evidence drill-down: every number clickable to source rows; export an auditor package (statements, reconciliations, schedules, approvals).\n c) Missing-accrual detector: flag recurring vendors with no entry this period.\n d) Policy memory: reuse approved resolutions via similarity search, always labeled \"from prior approval\" and overridable.\n e) Days-to-close scoreboard versus a manual baseline the user enters.\n f) Firm workspace: client status board and white-label board pack.\n g) Transparent pricing page with an editable ROI calculator and the guarantee \"pay only when checks pass and you approve\".\n13. GROWTH TOOLS: design-partner invite link, in-app feedback form, pilot tracker with empty fields, founder admin dashboard (closes, accuracy, revenue from billing_events, cost per close)..\n16. 60-second guided demo: upload, run close, review exception, approve, export board package PDF.\n\nDEFINITION OF DONE: tests pass, no hardcoded metrics, every placeholder labeled. End with a table: feature / real / simulated / not built. Ask me anything to include that my competitior like numeric rillet floquast and other similar digits Aren\'t paying attention ### SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE DIRECTIVE: AI STUDIO EXECUTION ENVIRONMENT\n- *Core Engine Execution:* The AI Studio execution environment runs all core business logic, matching algorithms, financial waterfalls, and invariant checks via deterministic local TypeScript engines. \n- *External Services Abstraction:* All external services\342\200\224including PostgreSQL vector extensions (pgvector), Stripe live network endpoints, and Cloud storage signed URL generators\342\200\224are fully implemented behind production-ready TypeScript abstractions, interfaces, and mock-safe service layers to guarantee robust execution and zero brittle third-party runtime dependencies within the sandbox.\n-"
    items {
      text: "Continue the existing FrogeClose app. Do NOT delete working code. Keep the dark UI. First list what is done / partial / not started, then build everything below IN ORDER in this one session. Never invent customers, traction, revenue, or testimonials. Show a \"Prototype on synthetic data\" badge. If AI Studio cannot run something for real, implement it behind an interface, say so clearly, and output the production version (schema.sql, config) too.\n\nCODE QUALITY RULES (enforced)\n- TypeScript strict, input validation (zod) on every API route, centralized error handling, environment variables only for secrets, no secrets in frontend code.\n- ALL security checks run on the server. UI hiding is never security.\n- Write automated tests for: reconciliation, ASC 606 schedule, ASC 340-40 schedule, the 5 invariants, role permissions, tenant isolation, Stripe webhook idempotency, audit hash chain. Show test results.\n\n1. AUTH AND TENANCY: signup/login behind an AuthProvider interface (Supabase Auth or Clerk swappable), organizations, memberships, roles Controller / Reviewer / Read-only enforced server-side. Accounting-firm mode: one user manages multiple client orgs.\n2. DATABASE: schema.sql (Postgres + pgvector + Row Level Security) for orgs, users, memberships, jobs, job_steps, files, bank_transactions, ledger_entries, stripe_payouts, matches, exceptions, journal_proposals, audit_logs, billing_events, evaluation_results, knowledge_base. Every table has org_id; repository layer always filters by org_id.\n3. FILES: CSV/PDF upload with type/size limits, checksums, signed-URL-style access, PII redaction option, sample CSV downloads (bank, ledger, Stripe payouts).\n4. BACKGROUND JOBS: async closes with queued/running/succeeded/failed, retries with backoff, idempotency key per close, progress polling.\n5. AGENT STATE MACHINE: Plan, Ingest, Reconcile, Draft, Verify, Exceptions, Finalize. Log each transition with input, output, confidence, duration, cost.\n6. DETERMINISTIC ENGINE (plain code, no LLM): reconciliation (normalize, hash-join on amount + date window, score ambiguous pairs, resolve by bipartite matching); recognized revenue + deferred revenue waterfall (ASC 606); ARR = MRR x 12 shown separately; commissions capitalized and amortized (ASC 340-40); checks with real pass/fail numbers: debits = credits, trial balance ties to statements, balance sheet balances, subledger ties to GL, no duplicate entries. The LLM only classifies ambiguous items and drafts commentary. It can never mark work as passed.\n7. EXCEPTIONS AND CONFIDENCE GATING: items above the threshold auto-resolve; below go to the Exception Inbox with proposed journal entry, confidence, Approve/Reject. Human override and rollback of any resolution.\n8. AUDIT TRAIL: every action logged with timestamp, actor, input, output, approver, hash of previous entry. \"Verify chain\" button detects tampering.\n9. STRIPE (test mode): Checkout plus webhook with signature verification, billing per verified close. Bill only if all checks pass AND a Controller approves. Idempotency keys, no double charge, automatic void/refund when a check fails, invoices and usage per org, first close free.\n10. SECURITY AND COST CONTROL: per-org rate limits and cost caps, input sanitization, \"What if the AI is wrong?\" panel.\n11. OBSERVABILITY AND EVALUATION: error logging, cost and time per close. Evaluation tab: 200 synthetic transactions with known answers (about 10% deliberate problems); compute accuracy, false positives, false negatives from the run, never hardcoded.\n12. DIFFERENTIATORS:\n a) Stripe payout tie-out explaining fees, refunds, disputes, FX and timing to the cent.\n b) Evidence drill-down: every number clickable to source rows; export an auditor package (statements, reconciliations, schedules, approvals).\n c) Missing-accrual detector: flag recurring vendors with no entry this period.\n d) Policy memory: reuse approved resolutions via similarity search, always labeled \"from prior approval\" and overridable.\n e) Days-to-close scoreboard versus a manual baseline the user enters.\n f) Firm workspace: client status board and white-label board pack.\n g) Transparent pricing page with an editable ROI calculator and the guarantee \"pay only when checks pass and you approve\".\n13. GROWTH TOOLS: design-partner invite link, in-app feedback form, pilot tracker with empty fields, founder admin dashboard (closes, accuracy, revenue from billing_events, cost per close)..\n16. 60-second guided demo: upload, run close, review exception, approve, export board package PDF.\n\nDEFINITION OF DONE: tests pass, no hardcoded metrics, every placeholder labeled. End with a table: feature / real / simulated / not built. Ask me anything to include that my competitior like numeric rillet floquast and other similar digits Aren\'t paying attention ### SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE DIRECTIVE: AI STUDIO EXECUTION ENVIRONMENT\n- *Core Engine Execution:* The AI Studio execution environment runs all core business logic, matching algorithms, financial waterfalls, and invariant checks via deterministic local TypeScript engines. \n- *External Services Abstraction:* All external services\342\200\224including PostgreSQL vector extensions (pgvector), Stripe live network endpoints, and Cloud storage signed URL generators\342\200\224are fully implemented behind production-ready TypeScript abstractions, interfaces, and mock-safe service layers to guarantee robust execution and zero brittle third-party runtime dependencies within the sandbox.\n-"
    }
  }
}
