  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User\'s Core Request:** Comprehensive enterprise expansion of FrogeClose (autonomous monthly close software for tech startups & accounting firms) while retaining the existing dark-mode UI, existing functional code, and strictly using synthetic data with a prominent `\"Prototype on synthetic data\"` badge.\n- **Key Deliverables & Specifications:**\n  1. Initial audit checklist: explicit list of Done / Partial / Not Started.\n  2. Implement features strictly in order (1 through 16):\n     - **1. Auth & Tenancy:** Signup/login interface (`AuthProvider` supporting Clerk/Supabase switchable via interface), multi-tenant organizations, accounting-firm mode (one user managing multiple client orgs), server-enforced roles (`controller`, `reviewer`, `read_only`).\n     - **2. Database Schema:** Complete production `schema.sql` (PostgreSQL + pgvector + Row Level Security, org_id filtering on every table).\n     - **3. Files & Storage:** CSV/PDF upload with MIME/size limits, SHA-256 checksums, signed-URL abstraction, PII redaction toggle, sample CSV downloads.\n     - **4. Background Jobs:** Async close runner with state transitions (`queued`, `running`, `succeeded`, `failed`), exponential backoff retries, idempotency key per close, progress polling.\n     - **5. Agent State Machine:** 7-stage engine (`Plan`, `Ingest`, `Reconcile`, `Draft`, `Verify`, `Exceptions`, `Finalize`) with logged durations, confidence scores, and token/compute cost.\n     - **6. Deterministic Engine (Plain TypeScript, No LLM Grading):**\n       - Bipartite matching + hash-join on amount & date window for bank vs GL.\n       - ASC 606 revenue recognition waterfall & separate ARR display (`ARR = MRR * 12`).\n       - ASC 340-40 sales commission capitalization ($60k capitalized, 48-month ratable amortization).\n       - 5 Deterministic GAAP Invariants with real numeric evaluation (Debits == Credits, Trial Balance Ties, Balance Sheet Identity, Subledger Ties to GL, Suspense Account Cleared / No Duplicates).\n     - **7. Exceptions & Confidence Gating:** Auto-resolve above confidence threshold; items below route to Controller Review Inbox; human override & rollback.\n     - **8. Audit Trail:** SHA-256 hash-chained log with tamper detection (\"Verify Chain\" button).\n     - **9. Stripe (Test Mode):** Checkout session generator, webhook handler with signature validation, conditional billing ($499/close, bill only if invariants pass AND Controller approves, first close free, automatic void/refund if failed).\n     - **10. Security & Cost Controls:** Per-tenant rate limits & cost caps, input sanitization with Zod, and interactive \"What if the AI is wrong?\" safety panel.\n     - **11. Observability & Real Evaluation:** Evaluation suite with 200 synthetic transactions (~10% deliberate anomalies) that computes dynamic Accuracy, False Positive, and False Negative rates from real run results (no hardcoded metrics).\n     - **12. Differentiators:**\n       - a) Stripe payout tie-out explaining fees, refunds, disputes, FX & timing to the penny.\n       - b) Evidence drill-down: clickable numbers to raw transaction rows + Auditor Package exporter.\n       - c) Missing-accrual detector: flagging recurring vendors missing in current period.\n       - d) Policy memory: similarity-matching approved prior journal entries with \"from prior approval\" tags.\n       - e) Days-to-close scoreboard vs manual baseline.\n       - f) Accounting-firm workspace: multi-client status board & white-label board packs.\n       - g) Transparent pricing page with interactive ROI calculator and money-back guarantee.\n     - **13. Growth Tools:** Design-partner invite generator, feedback modal, pilot tracker, and founder KPI dashboard.\n     - **14. 60-Second Guided Demo:** Fast interactive walkthrough covering upload, run, exception approval, verification, and PDF/MD export.\n  3. **Automated Test Suite:** Plain Node/Vitest automated tests verifying: reconciliation matching, ASC 606 waterfall, ASC 340-40 amortization, 5 invariants, role gating, tenant isolation, Stripe webhook idempotency, and audit hash chain verification.\n  4. **Definition of Done Table:** A markdown summary table classifying every item as `Real`, `Simulated`, or `Not Built`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Previous Turns:**\n  - `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`: Full React Context provider implementing multi-role authentication (`controller`, `reviewer`, `read_only`), active personas (`Elena Rostova, CPA`, `Marcus Vance`, `Sarah Sterling`), accounting firm multi-client switching (`Acme SaaS Inc`, `Nordic Cloud AS`, `Metis AI Labs`), and the `requireController(actionName, onSuccess)` security gate.\n  - `src/components/OnboardingTour.tsx`: Finite state machine overlay for interactive onboarding with tab synchronization and keyboard navigation.\n  - `src/App.tsx`: Refactored to integrate `AuthProvider`, display the active user badge and role selector, role-gate exception actions with lock badges, and mount the tour modal.\n  - Build & Lint Verified: `tsc --noEmit` and `compile_applet` succeeded, committed in git commit `d58afcd`.\n- **In-Progress / Next to Build:**\n  - Backend and deterministic calculation modules in `src/server/` and `src/core/`:\n    - `src/core/deterministicEngine.ts`: Full plain-code reconciliation, bipartite matching, ASC 606 & ASC 340-40 waterfalls, 5 invariants calculation.\n    - `src/core/agentStateMachine.ts`: 7-stage state machine logging durations, cost, and outputs.\n    - `src/core/auditChain.ts`: SHA-256 chain calculation & verification.\n    - `src/core/evaluationEngine.ts`: 200 synthetic transaction benchmarking suite with real compute of Accuracy/FP/FN.\n    - `src/core/differentiators.ts`: Stripe payout penny tie-out, missing accruals detector, policy memory repository.\n    - `src/server/schema.sql`: Full PostgreSQL schema with pgvector, RLS, multi-tenant tables.\n    - `src/server/stripeService.ts`: Stripe test mode billing with webhook signature validation and conditional approval charges.\n    - `src/server/api.ts` or routes: Zod validation schemas for all actions and role checks.\n    - Automated tests file (`src/core/__tests__/engine.test.ts` or executable runner `src/core/runTests.ts`) to execute and display verified test results.\n    - Integration of all differentiators and firm workspaces into UI tabs in `src/App.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Architecture Decisions\n- **AI Studio Environment Execution:** AI Studio does not have active external PostgreSQL/Supabase or live Stripe webhooks connected by default; the architecture directive requires all core engines (matching, waterfall, invariants, audit hash, evaluation) to run locally in deterministic TypeScript. Production schemas (`schema.sql`) and cloud storage/Stripe signatures are implemented with rigorous interfaces and clean simulation layers where third-party networks are unavailable.\n- **Security Check Rule:** All security checks (role checks, tenant checks) must be implemented with server/engine validation, never purely hidden in the UI. Non-controller actions must reject with `403 Forbidden` / `AuthorizationError`.\n- **Zero Hallucinated Metrics:** Accuracy, FP/FN in the evaluation tab must run across the 200 synthetic records and dynamically sum the results; no hardcoded static strings.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error:** TS17008: JSX element \'div\' has no corresponding closing tag in `src/App.tsx` (line 2917).\n  - *Fix:* Added the missing closing `</div>` to the footer container.\n- **Error:** TS2451: Duplicate declaration of `canApprove` in `src/App.tsx`.\n  - *Fix:* Replaced redundant local `const canApprove` with the context-provided `canApprove` and `canReview = canComment` from `useAuth()`.\n- **Build Status:** Verified passing with `lint_applet` and `compile_applet`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Root Directory:** `/` (shell working directory `/app/applet`).\n- **Dependencies Installed:** `lucide-react`, `recharts`, `tailwindcss`.\n- **Git State:** Clean working tree on commit `d58afcd`.\n- **Framework:** React SPA with Vite and TypeScript.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (Action Plan to Resume)\n1. **Present Initial Status Audit:**\n   - Output the explicit Done / Partial / Not Started table in the response.\n2. **Implement Core Engine Modules:**\n   - Create `src/core/deterministicEngine.ts`:\n     - Bank vs GL reconciliation (hash-join on amount + \302\2613 day window, bipartite tie-breaking).\n     - ASC 606 revenue waterfall with deferred revenue schedule and distinct `ARR = MRR * 12`.\n     - ASC 340-40 sales commissions schedule ($60k total, 48-month straight-line amortization).\n     - 5 Real Mathematical Invariants (Debits == Credits, Trial Balance ties, Balance sheet balances, Subledger ties to GL, Suspense account zeroed).\n   - Create `src/core/auditChain.ts`:\n     - Compute SHA-256 for entries, verify chain integrity, inject/detect simulated tampering.\n   - Create `src/core/evaluationEngine.ts`:\n     - Generate 200 realistic transactions with ~10% anomalies (unmatched fee, duplicate deposit, timing lag).\n     - Run matching and compute dynamic Accuracy, Precision, Recall, False Positives, False Negatives.\n   - Create `src/core/differentiators.ts`:\n     - Stripe penny tie-out breakdown (gross sales, processing fee, refund deduction, dispute reserve, net payout).\n     - Missing accrual detector for SaaS vendors (e.g. Datadog, Slack, AWS).\n     - Policy memory with semantic tag matching.\n     - Days-to-close benchmark calculator (comparing against manual close input).\n3. **Database & Stripe Artifacts:**\n   - Create `src/server/schema.sql`: Complete PostgreSQL schema with RLS, pgvector, and multi-tenant constraints.\n   - Create `src/server/stripeService.ts`: Stripe test mode billing with idempotency and controller approval conditional trigger.\n4. **Automated Test Runner:**\n   - Create `src/core/runTests.ts` that runs tests for:\n     1. Reconciliation matching\n     2. ASC 606 waterfall\n     3. ASC 340-40 schedule\n     4. 5 deterministic invariants\n     5. Role permissions & server gating\n     6. Tenant isolation\n     7. Stripe webhook idempotency\n     8. Audit hash chain integrity & tamper detection\n   - Run tests and display output in the terminal/UI.\n5. **UI Integration in `src/App.tsx`:**\n   - Ensure the \"Prototype on synthetic data\" badge is prominently visible.\n   - Wire all tabs: Accounting Firm Workspace, Missing Accruals, Stripe Tie-Out, Policy Memory, Evaluation (with 200 live test rows), and Pricing ROI Calculator.\n   - Compile and verify with `compile_applet`.\n   - Conclude with the requested Feature / Real / Simulated / Not Built table.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must NOT delete working code or disrupt the dark aesthetic.\n- Must display `\"Prototype on synthetic data\"` badge.\n- Never invent real customer logos, testimonials, or fake metrics.\n- Keep execution deterministic (no LLM marking its own homework).\n- All security checks must be enforced at the logic/service layer.\n</summary>"
