uplicate journal entries. Show pass/fail per check with the actual numbers.\n- Never let the LLM mark its own work as passed. The LLM drafts; code verifies.\n\n4. REAL INPUT\n- Add a CSV upload for a general ledger and bank transactions. Provide a downloadable sample CSV.\n- Run reconciliation (matching bank vs ledger) on the uploaded data and show matched, unmatched and flagged items.\n- Send only the flagged items to the Exception Inbox with a proposed fix, a confidence score, and Approve / Reject buttons.\n\n5. ACCURACY PROOF\n- Add an \"Evaluation\" tab: run the agent on 200 synthetic transactions with known correct answers. Show match accuracy, false positives, false negatives, and average time and cost per close. Compute these from the run, not hardcoded.\n\n6. TRUST AND AUDITABILITY\n- Make the Immutable Audit Trail log every agent action with timestamp, input, output, who approved, and a hash of the previous entry.\n- Add role permissions (Controller, Reviewer, Read-only) that actually change what the user can do.\n- Add a \"What if the AI is wrong?\" panel covering human override, rollback, and confidence thresholds.\n\n7. INVESTOR PAGES\n- Add a \"Competition\" tab comparing FrogeClose with FloQast, BlackLine, Numeric, Rillet and a manual controller, covering target customer, pricing, automation level and weakness. Mark clearly that the data should be verified.\n- Add a \"Market and Pricing\" tab with a transparent calculation: price per close, number of target SaaS companies, and the resulting revenue potential, with every assumption editable.\n- Add a \"Traction\" tab with empty fields for customer interviews, pilots, and letters of intent that I will fill in.\n\n8. QUALITY\n- Remove duplicate or decorative tabs that add no value.\n- Make everything responsive and fix text truncated with \"...\".\n- Add loading, error and empty states.\n- Add a 60-second guided demo mode that walks through: upload, agent runs, exceptions reviewed, board package exported.