  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Construction**\n\nI\'m currently assessing the completed, partially completed, and unstarted components, based on the prior request. Then I\'ll focus on finishing the pending items sequentially. I\'m keeping a close eye on the prompt instructions to ensure I keep all the numbers consistent across tabs.\n\n\n**Prioritizing the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the architectural design. I\'m focusing on the \"Auth and Tenancy\" component first, building it around an `AuthProvider` interface for flexibility. It\'s built in TypeScript, with strict mode enabled, alongside zod input validation. Security is server-side. Automated tests are planned for role permissions and tenant isolation. The UI design will be kept dark.\n\n\n**Defining the Core Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core feature set. The focus is now on read-only server-side enforcement. I\'m implementing an \"accounting-firm mode\" to support managing client orgs via a single user. I\'m outlining the Postgres database schema, incorporating pgvector and Row Level Security. I\'m building out file upload capabilities, including CSV/PDF support, size limits, checksums, and PII redaction.\n\n\n**Implementing the Financials**\n\nI\'m now integrating financial reporting and control mechanisms. I\'m focusing on revenue recognition according to ASC 606, including revenue waterfalls. I\'m ensuring ARR and MRR calculations are separate. Capitalized commissions and amortization will adhere to ASC 340-40. Checks will include debits equaling credits, and trial balance integrity. I\'m now incorporating a system that addresses potential issues.\n\n\n**Developing the Evaluation**\n\nI\'m now integrating observability and evaluation measures. I\'m focusing on incorporating error logging, cost/time analysis per close, and an evaluation tab. The evaluation tab will contain 200 synthetic transactions with known answers (10% with problems). I\'m planning to compute accuracy, false positives, and negatives from each run. The goal is no hardcoding.\n\n\n**Integrating the Feedback**\n\nI\'m now integrating feedback collection and pilot tracking features. I\'m focusing on a link, an in-app feedback form, and a pilot tracker with empty fields, along with a founder admin dashboard. The dashboard will track closes, accuracy, revenue from billing events, and cost per close. I\'m working on a 60-second guided demo that will cover upload, run close, exception review, approval, and export of a board package PDF. I\'m building with tests, no hardcoded metrics, and labeled placeholders. I am working on the definition of done with a table format. Finally, I\'ll be asking questions to identify the competition.\n\n\n**Calculating the Deterministics**\n\nI\'m now calculating 5 deterministic GAAP invariants dynamically. These invariants include checks for debits and credits, balance sheet identity, trial balance tie-out, subledger to GL tie-out, and zero suspense/duplicate detection. My approach involves string normalization, amount-based hash-joining with a date window for bank reconciliation, revenue waterfalls, and sales commission amortization.\n\n\n**Implementing the Cryptography**\n\nI\'m now implementing secure chain hashing using SHA-256 for integrity. This involves creating a `verifyChain` function to detect tampering and a `tamperBlock` function for testing. The chain is constructed with the hash of the index, timestamp, actor, action, and hashes of other data. I\'m moving toward deterministic security measures.\n\nI\'m generating synthetic transactions for the evaluation engine, including anomaly injection. I\'ll dynamically calculate performance metrics. Then I\'ll be implementing stripe payout tie-out.\n\n\n**Generating the Summaries**\n\nI\'m now generating financial summaries from multiple sources. I have accounted for every penny, including fees, refunds, and deposits. I\'m building a missing accrual detector to find missing entries for recurring vendors. I\'m also implementing policy memory to retrieve historical exception approvals. Furthermore, I\'ll be creating a days-to-close scoreboard and an auditor package generator.\n\n\n**Exporting the Fin-Tech Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on clean exporting. I\'m generating JSON/Markdown exports that include balance sheet, P&L, ASC schedules, bank reconciliation, audit trail hash chain, and controller sign-offs. I\'m building out a test mode Stripe integration, including mock and production webhook verification, ensuring charges only occur with both controller approval and all invariants passing. The charge will include idempotency keys, as well as automatic void/refunds. Finally, I\'m building out server routes with zod validation, role checking, rate limiters, and cost caps.\n\n\n**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI. I\'ve added a \"Prototype on synthetic data\" badge and expanded tabs to highlight differentiators: Stripe payout tie-out, missing accruals, policy memory, and days-to-close scoreboard. I\'m building a multi-client status board with close status, pending exceptions, and a white-label board pack preview for the firm workspace. I\'m also including a live benchmark with 200 transactions.\n\n\n"
