  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on identifying potential components and helpers to add to `src/App.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m thinking of importing `runAllAutomatedTests` and `FullTestSuiteReport` from `./core/runTests`, along with `runEvaluationBenchmark` and `EvaluationMetrics` from `./core/evaluationEngine`. Next, I\'ll figure out how to best integrate a `calculate` method, perhaps from a utilities directory.\n\n\n**Integrating Core Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on importing and integrating several key components from the `./core` and `./core/differentiators` directories into `src/App.tsx`. I\'ll be bringing in `StripePennyTieOut`, `detectMissingAccruals`, and `queryPolicyMemory`. I\'m also preparing state variables within `AppContent` for different tabs and differentiator sub-tabs. Specifically, I\'m setting up state for `testSuiteReport`, `isRunningTests`, and `evalMetrics`, initialized with `runEvaluationBenchmark`. Furthermore, I\'ll initialize several differentiator state variables such as `stripeTieOut`, `missingAccruals`, and `policyQuery`.\n\n\n**Defining App State**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the `App` component\'s state to include crucial data. I\'m initializing `policyList` using `queryPolicyMemory`, setting a `manualDaysBaseline` to 14, and calculating `daysScoreboard`. I\'ve also added state variables for `drillDownData`, `showGuidedDemoModal`, `guidedDemoStep`, `isAuditTampered`, and `auditVerificationResult`. Next, I\'ll integrate these into the UI and handle their interactions.\n\n\n\n**Structuring Financial Data**\n\nI\'m now organizing the financial data from a recent transaction. I\'ve noted the initial deposit, various fees, refunds, disputes, and variances. I\'m also preparing for the double-entry journal preview. I\'m building out sub-tabs, including a Missing-Accrual Detector that flags missing entries, a Policy Memory with similarity scores and tags, and a Days-to-Close Scoreboard with an editable baseline and ROI calculations. Finally, I\'m working on the rendering for the \'firm_workspace\' tab, building a multi-client status board, a white-label board pack generator, and a design partner pilot tracker.\n\n\n**Implementing Test Automation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the test automation components. Within the \'verification\' tab, I\'ll add the \"Run All 8 Automated Test Suites\" button, which will execute `runAllAutomatedTests()` and display test results. The \'evaluation\' tab will incorporate the \'evalMetrics\' and a 200-transaction ground-truth table. I\'m also planning the functionality for the \'audit\' tab, which includes a SHA-256 hash chain verification and a tampering simulation. Finally, I\'m working on the design for the Evidence Drill-Down Drawer, triggered by row clicks in P&L and Balance Sheet tables.\n\n\n"
