  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Implementation**\n\nI\'m focusing on the `activeTab === \'verification\'` scenario. I\'ve pinpointed lines 2865-2869 for replacement, and I plan to integrate those 5 checks and the Automated Test Runner panel there. This should streamline the verification process, keeping it concise and efficient.\n\n\n**Integrating Test Suite**\n\nI\'m currently integrating the automated test suite panel. My focus is on dynamically updating the interface to display test results. The plan involves conditionally rendering the report and managing the `isRunningTests` state to ensure the user experience is smooth and informative. I will leverage the test results to improve the user\'s validation experience.\n\n\n**Updating Test Panel**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the test panel button and report display logic. I\'m dynamically adjusting the button\'s content based on the `isRunningTests` state and efficiently rendering test results with a concise display. This ensures that the user can get clear feedback at every stage.\n\n\n**Displaying Results Clearly**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying the test results within the panel. I\'m aiming for a concise and easily digestible format. The approach involves iterating through the test results and rendering each test\'s suite, name, and duration. For successful tests, I\'ll use a clear \"PASS\" label with a green color, ensuring immediate clarity for the user. I\'ll also add a timestamp for the last verification.\n\n\n**Adding Evaluation Feature**\n\nI\'m now implementing the evaluation feature, and I\'m updating the `handleRunEvaluation` function to include an `isEvaluating` state and a timed execution to simulate the evaluation. I will also incorporate the 200 Synthetic Txn Sample Inspector table, displaying 30 anomalies and normal transactions to showcase evaluation capabilities.\n\n\n**Implementing Audit Tamper**\n\nI\'m now implementing the audit tamper feature using `setIsAuditTampered` to simulate tampering. I\'m dynamically updating the UI with a button that toggles between simulating and detecting tampering on block #2. I\'m also ensuring the tamper state is reflected in the button text and class names.\n\n\n"
